hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2005","(2005) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He used to say: The socks and sandals are in the same place as the socks, He did not think that one of them should be wiped over rather than the other."
"2006","(2006) Waki` told us, he said: Abu Ja`far al-Razi told us, on the authority of Yahya al-Bakai, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: Wiping over the socks is like wiping over the socks."
"2007","(2007) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Zaid; That Ali urinated and wiped on his sandals."
"2008","(2008) Abu Bakr told us: On the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Sudair, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: He should not wipe over the sandals."
"2009","(2009) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, on the authority of Aws bin Abi Aws, who said: I ended up with my father to a hundred people. The water of the Bedouins, so he performed ablution and wiped over his shoes, so I said to him? He said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, do it.\n(Abu Dawud 161, Ahmad 4/10, Ibn Hibban 1339)"
"2010","(2010) Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Idris, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, who said: I saw Ali standing, Then he performed ablution and wiped over his sandals, then the muezzin stood up and he took them off."
"2011","(2011) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, on the authority of Ukil, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafali; That Ali urinated and wiped on his sandals."
"2012","(2012) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan; He saw Ali urinating in the spacious room, then he performed ablution and wiped over his sandals."
"2013","(2013) Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Idris, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, who said: I saw on Ibrahim Two scarves from Labud, he wiped over them."
"2014","(2014) Abu Bakr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Mubarak, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that in a state of sexual intercourse there is sweat in the garment until Is it squeezed? He said: He prays in it."
"2015","(2015) Hushaym told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He saw no harm in the sweat of a woman who was in a state of impurity or menstruating women."
"2016","(2016) Hushaym told us, saying: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He saw no harm in the sweat of a woman who was in a state of impurity or menstruating women."
"2017","(2017) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; During a state of sexual impurity, he sweats on his garment, takes his sweat and wipes it with it: he sees no harm in it."
"2018","(2018) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He saw no harm in the sweat of a woman who was in a state of impurity or menstruating women."
"2019","(2019) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha; She did not see any harm in the sweat of one who was in a state of sexual impurity."
"2020","(2020) Yahya bin Sulaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He did not see any harm in the sweat of one who is in a state of impurity. The garment, and there is no impurity on it."
"2021","(2021) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’; I asked Hammad about a menstruating woman who sweats in her clothes. Should she wash her clothes? He said: Only the Magi do that."
"2022","(2022) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He was sweating in his garment while he was in ritual state, then he would pray in it."
"2023","(2023) Hatem bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of alcohol; He did not see any harm in sweating on his clothes."
"2024","(2024) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, he said: There is no harm in the sweat of a junub person. In the dress."
"2025","(2025) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim; Is he sweating in his clothes during his side? He said: He will not harm him, nor will he sprinkle water on him."
"2026","(2026) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Zubaid, and Al-Amash, who said: Ibrahim used to go to the door of the mosque. In his sandals, or in his socks, he wipes them over, then goes in and prays."
"2027","(2027) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Asim bin Al-Mundhir; I asked Urwah bin Al-Zubair about dung getting on the soles? He said: Wipe it and pray over it."
"2028","(2028) Waki’ told us on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Thabit ibn Ubaid, who said: I saw him scratching his sandal or shoe at a door. The mosque, he said: It is mentioned that it is pure."
"2029","(2029) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Hammad, who said: They used to struggle with wet dung when He was in secret."
"2030","(2030) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Karim, who said: A peacock was dear to me when he entered the mosque. He does not turn over his socks or sandals."
"2031","(2031) Hushaym told us, saying: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far and Ata’; Indeed, they saw no harm in the blood of fleas and mosquitoes."
"2032","(2032) Hisham told us, he said: Ash’ath bin Siwar told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he said: Al-Hasan did not see the blood of flies. And mosquitoes and fleas are miserable."
"2033","(2033) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, who said: I prayed and there was fly blood on my garment, so I said to my father? He said: It will not harm you."
"2034","(2034) Al-Fadl bin Dukain told us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir and Ata’, who said: There is no harm in the blood of fleas."
"2035","(2035) Zajir bin Al-Salt narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Malik, who said: I went to Al-Hasan’s house, and a man came and asked him, and he said: O Abu Saeed, a man spends the night in his clothes, and in the morning there is a lot of flea blood in it, so he washes it, or Does he sprinkle it, or pray in it? He said: He does not sprinkle it, nor wash it, but pray in it."
"2036","(2036) Hushaym told us, saying: Hisham told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: There is no harm in the blood of fish, unless you make it dirty."
"2037","(2037) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Wash off any blood of the hunter that has come upon you."
"2038","(2038) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, saying: Ash’ath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he said about a person on ablution who passed by water without needing He performed ablution and completed it, and the time for prayer began, but he did not have any water with him. He said: He must repeat the tayammum, because his ability to reach the water invalidates his tayammum."
"2039","(2039) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Vomit, wine, and blood are in the same place, meaning: In the dress"
"2040","(2040) Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If wine gets on your clothes So wash it, it is stronger than blood."
"2041","(2041) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin, that they said: There is no harm in sprinkling a woman’s impurity or a menstruating woman. The mosque"
"2042","(2042) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Anas; A Bedouin urinated in the mosque, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for some water and poured it over his urine. (Bukhari 221, Muslim 236)"
"2043","(2043) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Qays, who said: A Bedouin urinated in the mosque, so the Prophet ordered May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so he poured water on his urine."
"2044","(2044) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: A Bedouin entered The mosque and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in it. He urinated, so he ordered a bucket of water to be filled, and he emptied his urine on it.\n(Ahmad 2/503, Ibn Hibban 985)"
"2045","(2045) Yahya bin Isa al-Ramli told us, on the authority of Razin, who said: A man came to Abu Ja`far and said to him: I will go out. On a rainy night, do I step on mud? He said: Pray. He said: I fear that there will be stench and filth in it. It was as if he got angry. He said: If you are treading on the stench. Your feet, so take water with you and wash your feet with it."
"2046","(2046) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, that he said to a man: Have you not anointed them? And you entered."
"2047","(2047) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: Ali was wading through the mud of rain and entering the mosque. He prays but does not perform ablution."
"2048","(2048) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Hakim bin Al-Daylam, who said: I saw Ibn Maqil on a rainy day, standing and praying. To a woman in the mosque, and on her feet like anklets or stonecroppers."
"2049","(2049) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, who said: I saw Al-Qalamiyah and the lions wading through water. It was raining, and the gutters were gushing, then they entered the mosque and prayed but did not perform ablution."
"2050","(2050) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: When he entered the mosque in the rain, he looked at his socks. If there was a little mud on them, he wiped them off, then went in and washed them, and if there was a lot of mud, he took them off and ordered them to be washed."
"2051","(2051) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Our companions used to wade through water and mud to their mosques, and they pray but do not wash their feet."
"2052","(2052) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar bin Saad, who said: I saw Al-Qasim bin Muhammad entering the mosque on a rainy day, and he did not He washes his feet."
"2053","(2053) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I was wading through the rain, so I asked the judge? He said: Pray, pray.\n He said: And I heard Abu Ishaq say: They used to go out and then pray, and they did not carry cups with them."
"2054","(2054) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Amr bin Abdullah, who said: He was wearing a tail on his socks, then he would pray in them."
"2055","(2055) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: I passed with Ibn Sirin on a road, and a gutter dripped on it. So he asked about it, and it was said: It is clean, but he did not pay attention to it, and did not care about it."
"2056","(2056) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Mas’ad, who said: Abdullah Al-Rumi narrated to us, saying: Othman used to stand up from At night, he will clean his birds by himself, and it will be said to him: If I command some of the servants, and he will say: I would love to have him myself."
"2057","(2057) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Abdul Rahman Al-Madani, who said: There are two characteristics that did not... The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to give each of them to one of his family. He used to give food to the poor with his hand. And he puts on the ritual ablution at night and covers it. (Ibn Majah 362)"
"2058","(2058) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Mus`ab bin Shayba, on the authority of Talq, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Ten things that are unnatural: trimming the moustache, keeping the beard, and using the siwak. Inhaling water, cutting nails, washing knuckles, plucking armpits, shaving the pubic hair, and squeezing water. Musab said: And I forgot the tenth, unless it was rinsing the mouth. (Muslim 223. Ibn Majah 293)"
"2059","(2059) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: Five things are unnatural: circumcision, puberty, trimming the nails, plucking the armpits, and trimming the moustache.\n(Bukhari 5889. Muslim 221)"
"2060","(2060) Qubaisa bin Uqba told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Salama bin Muhammad, on the authority of Ammar Ibn Yasir said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Breaking the mouth is rinsing the mouth, sniffing the mouth, using the siwak, and trimming the moustache. Plucking the armpits, washing the toes, trimming the nails, rinsing oneself with water, and circumcision.\n(Abu Dawud 55. Ibn Majah 294)"
"2061","(2061) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Six of the innate actions of Abraham, peace be upon him: trimming the mustache, The siwak, the band, cutting the nails, cleaning oneself, and shaving the pubic hair. He said: Three in the head, and three in the body."
"2062","(2062) Muhammad bin Bishr Al-Abdi and Asamah narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Ayyub, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Indeed, Satan has phlegm, meaning: wetness at the tip of the urethra."
"2063","(2063) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: No person visited him except He saw something he disliked, or bad, meaning: wetness at the tip of the urethra."
"2064","(2064) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, who said: He wets the tip of the urethra."
"2065","(2065) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of a man from Quraysh, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl, who said: They were not checking that closely."
"2066","(2066) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, he said: He did not whisper to someone who was more deceitful than anyone. I see her working on it."
"2067","(2067) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Muslim bin Atiyya, who said: Tawoos said: And why did you look at your penis?"
"2068","(2068) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Ruwaybah, on the authority of Abu Umamah ibn Sahl, who said: What A man who mentioned that inspection checked on him, but he saw something he disliked."
"2069","(2069) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mufaddal bin Mihalil, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Tamim bin Salamah, he said: Ibn Al-Zubair said: Satan comes to man by means of ablution, hair, and nails."
"2070","(2070) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Ata’; Whoever forgets to rinse his mouth during ablution or to blow his nose, he said: He should rinse his mouth and nose and repeat the prayer."
"2071","(2071) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Aisha bint Ajrad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If a man prays He forgot to rinse his mouth and nose from his side, so he repeated his rinsing and nose."
"2072","(2072) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muthanna, on the authority of Ata’; If someone forgets to rinse his mouth and nose until he prays, he says: He does not have to repeat them."
"2073","(2073) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who forgets to rinse his mouth, he said: If he has entered the prayer, then let him rinse his mouth, and if he has not entered the prayer, then let him rinse his mouth. And let him inhale."
"2074","(2074) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A man repeats the prayer from Forgetting to rinse the mouth and nose."
"2075","(2075) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam, Hammad, and their followers about a man who forgets to rinse his mouth. And inhaling until one stands for prayer. Al-Hakam and his followers said: He should continue, and Hammad said: He should stop."
"2076","(2076) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, who said: If he forgets to rinse his mouth and nose in ritual impurity. He repeated it, and if he forgot during ablution, that is sufficient."
"2077","(2077) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, Concerning a man who forgot to rinse his mouth and nose until he prayed, he said: That does not count."
"2078","(2078) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, and Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Inhalation is not obligatory."
"2079","(2079) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Hammad, who said: If a man forgets to rinse his mouth and nose, then He celebrates"
"2080","(2080) Hassan bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I said to Ibrahim: A man forgets to inhale. So he mentions in prayer that he forgot? Ibrahim said: He continues his prayer. He said: And Mansour said: And rinsing the mouth is like that."
"2081","(2081) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: If some of the mothers Believers, the blood will be dripped from their garments with their sparkle."
"2082","(2082) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Yazid bin Ziyad, that Al-Hasan bin Ali saw blood on his shirt, He spit on it, then rubbed it."
"2083","(2083) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hussein bin Jaafar, he said: Salit bin Abdullah bin Yasar told me, he said: I saw Ibn Omar saw blood on his socks, so he spit on it, then rubbed it."
"2084","(2084) Khaled bin Hayyan told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, who said: I saw Maymun bin Mihran one day while he was praying. He saw blood on his clothes, so he said so and so about it, meaning: its sparkle, then he rubbed it with his hand."
"2085","(2085) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, Amir, and Ata’, they said: Blood is not washed off. With slugs"
"2086","(2086) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He saw blood on his garment, so he washed it, but a black trace remained. He called for a pair of scissors, cut it, and cut it off."
"2087","(2087) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Harith, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If you wash off the blood and traces of it remain, it will not harm you."
"2088","(2088) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Fadl bin Dulham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, a similar story."
"2089","(2089) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Karimah Ibn Hammam, she said: I heard Aisha, and she was asked about Does menstrual blood get on the clothes? She said: Wash it. She said: I washed it, but no traces of it left. So she said: Wash it, for the water is pure."
"2090","(2090) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who fainted while sitting, he said: He performs ablution."
"2091","(2091) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the afflicted person recovers, he should perform ablution."
"2092","(2092) Hussein bin Ali narrated to us, on the authority of Zayed, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, he said: Ubaid Allah bin Abd narrated to me Allah bin Utbah said: I came to Aisha and said: Tell me about the illness of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: Yes. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell ill and became heavy, so he fainted. Then he woke up and said: Put water for me in the trough. She said: So we did so. She said: So he took a bath, then he went to Nou’a and fainted. Then he woke up and said: Put water in the basin for me. She said: So we did so. She said: So he took a bath. So he went to sleep and fainted, then he woke up and said: Put water in the basin for him, so he took a bath. He even did it several times. (Bukhari 687. Muslim 311)"
"2093","(2093) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Asim bin Badlahi, on the authority of Musa bin Talhah; Othman used to wash himself several times every day."
"2094","(2094) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, on the authority of Ali, who said: To take a bath on the cold night."
"2095","(2095) Sulayman bin Harb narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father; He used to wash himself several times every day."
"2096","(2096) Suleiman bin Harb told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad; He used to wash himself several times every day."
"2097","(2097) Waki’ and Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salama, who said: Ali said: I take a bath on a cold night without being in a state of ritual impurity, so that I can clean myself with it and purify myself."
"2098","(2098) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Sakhrah Jami’ ibn Shaddad, who said: I heard Hamran ibn Aban, the servant of Uthman. Ibn Affan says: I used to add his toilet bowl for Uthman, and not a day came when he did not sprinkle some sperm on him. Of water"
"2099","(2099) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Farwa, who said: I went with Ibn Abi Layla to the Euphrates, and he entered him wearing a garment. Or he said: with an apron, and he said: he has a loincloth."
"2100","(2100) Al-Muharabi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, he said: I was told by someone who saw Husayn ibn Ali entering the water wearing a garment, and said: He has still"
"2101","(2101) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, who said: He narrated to me someone who saw Omar marshy in water with a shirt on, then He went out and called for a quilt and put it on over his shirt."
"2102","(2102) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Saad narrated to us, saying: Zayd bin Aslam narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Saad. Al-Jari, who was a servant of Omar, said: Omar came to us on the authority of Hajj, with a group of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: O Saad, we need handkerchiefs. He brought handkerchiefs and said: Bath in it, for it is blessed."
"2103","(2103) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Isa bin Hilal, on the authority of Kathir, the servant of Salama, who said: Whoever slaughters an animal, let him perform ablution."
"2104","(2104) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, Concerning a man who slaughters a camel or a sheep, he said: If blood gets on it, he should wash it, and he does not have to perform ablution."
"2105","(2105) Mus’ab bin Al-Miqdam told us, on the authority of Zayed, on the authority of Mughir, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If a man performs ablution and then He slaughtered a sheep, that did not interrupt his purification, and if blood got on it, he washed it, but if no blood got on it, then there is nothing wrong with him."
"2106","(2106) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, he said: I saw Ibrahim entering the toilet. He put on his socks, then he went out, performed ablution, and wiped over them."
"2107","(2107) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Omar bin Dharr narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin al-Harith, he said: I invited Ibrahim al-Nakha’i, And Ibrahim al-Taymi. They entered the toilet wearing their socks, then they came out. They performed ablution and wiped over their socks, then they prayed."
"2108","(2108) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of a man whom he did not name, on the authority of Ibrahim, and al-Hakam; When they wanted to urinate, they would put on their socks as if they would wipe them."
"2109","(2109) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: There is no ritual impurity on the garment."
"2110","(2110) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Abu Awani, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: The garment does not He avoids it."
"2111","(2111) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The garment does not make one avoid one’s body."
"2112","(2112) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man performing ablution and his ablution dries up. He said: If he was performing ablution, he washed his feet, and if he was not performing ablution, he washed his feet. Ablution resumed ablution."
"2113","(2113) Waki’ told us, he said: I asked Sufyan about that? He said: He should wash his feet. I said: What if his ablution dried up? He said: And if the ablution dries up, he said: And so we say"
"2114","(2114) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid (h) and on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; Indeed, they disliked that the word “junub” should be written: In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful."
"2115","(2115) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They did not see any harm in A man writes the letter without performing ablution."
"2116","(2116) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Sinan Dirar ibn Murra, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi al-Dhudhayl Al-Anazi, he said: They used to remember God in every state except during ritual impurity."
"2117","(2117) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, Amir, and Ata’, they said: There is nothing of Drinking is ablution."
"2118","(2118) Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Qalab; He gave them some wine to drink, so they performed ablution."
"2119","(2119) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In the case of amputation, if his leg was cut off at the joint and he wanted to perform ablution: he washed the cut, and if the hand was cut off, he washed up to The attachment"
"2120","(2120) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Zayd ibn Thabit suffered from urinary incontinence, and he used to pray without urinating."
"2121","(2121) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Salamah ibn Alqamiya, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: I was informed that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace A menstruating woman used to walk him, and he would say: Her menstruation is not in her hand."
"2122","(2122) Ibn Numayr and Ya’la ibn Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Tamim ibn Salama, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha. She said: I was touching the head of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while I was menstruating, and he was single. \n(Nasa’i 3383. Ahmad 6/32)"
"2123","(2123) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Perhaps a female slave performed ablution on him. One of her female slaves, who is menstruating, washes her feet."
"2124","(2124) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Omar; That a female servant was washing her feet while she was menstruating."
"2125","(2125) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was And he brought his head close to me while I was menstruating, and he is a mujawār, meaning: secluded, so he would place it on my lap, so I would wash it. And I have sex with him while I am menstruating.\n(Bukhari 2961, Muslim 244)"
"2126","(2126) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah; That Abu Dhabyan asked Abraham about a menstruating woman performing ablution for a sick woman? He said: There is no harm in it."
"2127","(2127) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in a menstruating woman washing a man’s head and foot."
"2128","(2128) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of an outcast, on the authority of his mother, who said: Ibn Abbas entered Maimuna, and she said: My son, why do I see you with your head disheveled? He said: Umm Ammar, my wife, is menstruating. She said: My son, where is menstruation from the hand? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to place his head in the lap of one of us while she was menstruating.\n(Nasa’i 267 Ahmad 6/331)"
"2129","(2129) Omar bin Ayyub Al-Mawsili told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; If a sick person is unable to perform ablution, he said: He should perform tayammum."
"2130","(2130) Abu Asama told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Qays bin Saad, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, And Mujahid, they said about the sick person being afflicted by impurity, and he fears for himself. He said: He is in the same position as a traveler who cannot find The watery person performs tayammum. I asked Ataa, and he said: It is necessary to have water and make it hot."
"2131","(2131) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, who said: The companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, told us; Abdullah bin Zayd Al-Ansari came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I saw in a dream It is as if a man stood up wearing two green robes on a wall, so he called the call to prayer in two, and made a double iqama, and sat down, saying: So Bilal heard that, so he stood up and gave the call to prayer, made the call to prayer, made the call to prayer, made a double call to prayer, and sat down. (Abu Dawud 507, Ibn Khuzaymah 380)"
"2132","(2132) Affan narrated to us, he said, Hammam bin Yahya narrated to us, on the authority of Amir Al-Ahwal, that Makhoul narrated to him, that Abdullah bin Muhayriz told him that Abu Mahdhur told him, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught me the nineteen times the call to prayer. A word and the Iqamah is seventeen words, the call to prayer: Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, I bear witness I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness That there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, alive On the blessings, hail on the prayers, hail on the success, hail on the success, God is great, God is great, there is no god but God.\n And the residence: Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. There is no god but God, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, may peace be upon him, may peace be upon him, may peace be upon him Ali Al-Falah, hail Ali Al-Falah, the prayer has begun, the prayer has begun, God is great, God is great, there is no god but God. (Abu Daw9 503. Tirmidhi 192)"
"2133","(2133) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: It was Ibn Umar’s call to prayer, God is Great, Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. God, three times, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, three times, may God bless him and grant him peace. Prayer, three times, Hail Al-Falah, three times, God is Great, I think he said: There is no god but God."
"2134","(2134) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: The call to prayer used to say: God is great, God is great. Akbar, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad The Messenger of God, may peace be upon him, may peace be upon him, may peace be upon him, may peace be upon him, may peace be upon him, may peace be upon him?? Al-Falah, Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is the greatest."
"2135","(2135) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, he said: Al-Hasan used to say: Allah is the greatest, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, he greeted the prayer, he greeted the farmer, then he comes back and says: God is great, God is great, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, Hail the Salat, Hail the Falah, twice, Allah The greatest, God is the greatest, there is no god but God."
"2136","(2136) Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: Sulayman al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Habib bin Qais, on the authority of Ibn Abi It is forbidden, on the authority of his father, that he used to lower his voice during the call to prayer time after time, until he ended by saying: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. He returned to his saying: I bear witness that there is no god but God. He raised With his voice twice, until when he ended with: “Hayyat al-Salaat,” he said: “Prayer is better than sleep,” in the call to prayer. The first day of dawn.\n(Abu Dawud 502. Ahmad 3/409)"
"2137","(2137) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, he said: Our companions narrated to us; A man from the Ansar came and said: O Messenger of God, when I returned yesterday and saw from your care, I saw as if A man standing in front of the mosque wearing two green garments gave the call to prayer, then he sat down, then he got up and said the same thing, except that he said: The prayer has begun, and had you not said it, I would have said: I was awake and not asleep. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I have May God bless you with goodness, so Omar said: As for me, I saw something like what he saw, except that when I came before, I became ashamed, so the Prophet said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Tell Bilal to give the call to prayer. (Abu Dawud 507)"
"2138","(2138) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said hello, in a similar way."
"2139","(2139) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Mahdhuriya; His call to prayer was two, and his iqama was one."
"2140","(2140) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: Bilal used to intercede for the call to prayer, And he performs the Iqamah Witr prayer. (Abu Dawud 511, An-Nasa’i 1593)"
"2141","(2141) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, he said: I think it is on the authority of Anas, he said: Bilal was commanded to recite the call to prayer. And the Iqamah is prayed Witr. (Muslim 2864, Ahmad 3/103)"
"2142","(2142) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, on the authority of Anas, who said: Bilal was commanded to recite the call to prayer, and to pray Witr. Residence (Bukhari 607 and Muslim 286)"
"2143","(2143) Abdou told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah; His father used to recite the call to prayer and recite the Iqamat Witr."
"2144","(2144) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, who said: The call to prayer is twofold, and the iqāmah is one."
"2145","(2145) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Taimiy, who said: A man in the Kufa Mosque narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, He said: The Iqamah is one. He said: Likewise is Bilal’s call to prayer."
"2146","(2146) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He used to say: Iqama is sometimes, so when he said: The prayer began, he said: twice."
"2147","(2147) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: I stayed with him in Dabiq, and he did not He adds more than one Iqamat, and does not call to prayer, and makes it one."
"2148","(2148) Abdi told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Al-Muthanna; That Ibn Omar used to order the muezzin to pronounce the adhan at the end of the call, and to pronounce the iqama on the odd vowel, so that the passer-by would know the adhan from the iqama."
"2149","(2149) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yahya, on the authority of al-Hajna’ ibn Qays; That Ali used to say: The call to prayer is twofold and the Iqamah is twofold, and a muezzin came to me, performing the iqama, one after the other, and said: Haven’t you made it twofold? There is no mother for the other."
"2150","(2150) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Ismail, on the authority of Ubaid Mawla Salma bin Al-Akwa’; That Salama bin Al-Akwa’ used to make the Iqamah second."
"2151","(2151) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, he said: Abdullah bin Zaid Al-Ansari was the muezzin of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who would intercede for the call to prayer and the iqamah.\n(Tirmidhi 194, Dar Qatni 241)"
"2152","(2152) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, who said: If you make it He established it and then he continued it."
"2153","(2153) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Do not let anything dissuade you. Residence"
"2154","(2154) Affan told us, he said: Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, he said: Al-Hajjaj bin Arta told us, he said: Abu Ishaq, he said: The companions of Ali and the companions of Abdullah used to intercede for the call to prayer and the iqama."
"2155","(2155) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Bilal used to give the call to prayer. And the residence.\n(Abdul Razzaq 1791, Dar Qatni 35)"
"2156","(2156) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, who said: Bilal’s last call to prayer was: There is no god but God (Nasa’i 1615, Dar Qatni 244)"
"2157","(2157) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Al-Shu’bi, who said: Bilal’s last call to prayer was: By God. The greatest, God is the greatest, there is no god but God."
"2158","(2158) Abu Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Abu Mahdour: He gave the call to prayer to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted Abu Bakr and Omar, and his last adhan was: Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, there is no god but Allah."
"2159","(2159) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, who said: Qaid Abi Mahdhur narrated to me, with something similar."
"2160","(2160) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Abbas narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Mahdhuriya saying in His last call to prayer: Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, there is no god but Allah, except that his call to prayer was double, and his iqama was One, and the end of his call to prayer: Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, there is no god but Allah."
"2161","(2161) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Mahdhuriya, with a similar story."
"2162","(2162) Abd Allah bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Ubad Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to make his last adhan: Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, there is no god but Allah."
"2163","(2163) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Abbas narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Mahdhuriya, saying in His last adhan: Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, there is no god but Allah."
"2164","(2164) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, who said: I heard Ibrahim, saying: The last call to prayer is Allahu Akbar, Allah is the Greatest. There is no god but Allah."
"2165","(2165) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abu Sadiq; He used to make his last call to prayer: There is no god but Allah, and God is great, and he said: This is how Bilal’s last call to prayer was."
"2166","(2166) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Yazid, on the authority of Abi Forbidden, he said: The last call to prayer was: Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, there is no god but Allah. (Nasa’i 1616)"
"2167","(2167) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Bilal, he said: There was another The call to prayer: Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, there is no god but Allah. (Nasa’i 1614)"
"2168","(2168) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, he said: It was the last adhan. He refused, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave him the call to prayer in Mecca, and his last call to prayer was: God is Great. God is Great, there is no god but God."
"2169","(2169) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abu Sahl, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It was the last adhan. Bilal: God is great, God is great, there is no god but God."
"2170","(2170) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Mahdhuriya (h) and on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Suwayd, on the authority of Bilal; It was their last prayer: Prayer is better than sleep. (Abu Dawud 5051 Ibn Khuzaymah)"
"2171","(2171) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafali; He sent to his muezzin: When you reach Ali Al-Falah, say: Prayer is better than sleep, for it is Bilal’s call to prayer."
"2172","(2172) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of a man called: Ismail, who said: He came The muezzin called Omar to the morning prayer, and he said: Prayer is better than sleep. So Omar was impressed with him, and he said to the muezzin: Recite it in... Your ears"
"2173","(2173) Abdullah told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to say in his call to prayer: Prayer is better than sleep."
"2174","(2174) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: He said: It is not Sunnah to say in the Fajr prayer: Prayer is better than sleep. (Ibn Khuzaymah 386. Dar Qatni 38)"
"2175","(2175) Abdi narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, he said: Bilal came to the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He was calling to prayer, and it was said to him: He is sleeping, so Bilal shouted at the top of his voice: Prayer. It is better than sleep, so it was included in the call to prayer. (Ibn Majah 716)"
"2176","(2176) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah; That his father used to say in his call to prayer: Prayer is better than sleep, prayer is better than sleep, God is great, God is great. There is no god but Allah."
"2177","(2177) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abi Mukhaymara, that he used to say Concerning his call to prayer in the words: Prayer is better than sleep, prayer is better than sleep."
"2178","(2178) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad, who said: The ta-thawb used to say: alive. On prayer, prayer is better than sleep."
"2179","(2179) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Hakim bin Jubayr, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Yazid He heard a muezzin saying at dawn: Prayer is better than sleep, so he said: Do not add anything to the call to prayer that is not part of it."
"2180","(2180) Abu Khalid Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Abu Mahdhuriya; He gave the call to prayer to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and to Abu Bakr and Omar, and he used to say in his call to prayer: Prayer is better. From sleep"
"2181","(2181) Yahya bin Abi Bakr told us, he said: Ali bin Al-Harith told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim, he said: I heard Muezzin Omar bin Abdul Aziz says: Prayer is better than sleep."
"2182","(2182) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Khaythami, who said: They used to dress themselves during the evening prayer. And dawn."
"2183","(2183) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn al-Asbaani, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, who said: What They invented an innovation that is more beloved to me than the tathwib in prayer, meaning: Isha and Fajr."
"2184","(2184) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Mahdhuriya (h) and on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Suwayd, on the authority of Bilal; They did not dress except at dawn."
"2185","(2185) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafali; He sent to him a muezzin called Rabah: not to pronounce the garment except at dawn."
"2186","(2186) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to dress themselves during the night prayer. And dawn."
"2187","(2187) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Izza, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He wears a garment for the evening prayer. And dawn."
"2188","(2188) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to dress during the darkness and dawn, and it was The muezzin of Abraham called at noon and afternoon, but he did not prohibit it."
"2189","(2189) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Aoun bin Abi Juhayfy, on the authority of his father; Bilal mounted the goat and called the call to prayer, and I saw him turning to say the call to prayer. (Tirmidhi 1971, Ahmad 4/308)"
"2190","(2190) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: When the muezzin gives the call to prayer, he faces the qiblah. And he hated to turn around in the minaret.\n Al-Hasan used to say: Facing towards the qiblah, so when he said: Hail to the prayer, he would turn around, and when he wanted to say: God is Great, Facing the Qiblah."
"2191","(2191) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ar-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan (H), on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, they said: The muezzin does not remove his feet."
"2192","(2192) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Awn ibn Abi Juhaif, on the authority of his father, who said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, peace be upon him, with Al-Abtah. Then Bilal came out and called the call to prayer. He said: It is as if I am looking at Him following His mouth, here and here. Meaning: right and left.\n(Bukhari 634, Muslim 360)"
"2193","(2193) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The muezzin recites the call to prayer. And the Shahadah and the Qiblah."
"2194","(2194) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hallam bin Salih, on the authority of Faid bin Bukair, who said: I went out with Hudhayfah to the mosque. Fajr prayer, and Ibn al-Tayyah is the muezzin, and al-Walid ibn Uqba gives the call to prayer, and he says: Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. He gave his call to prayer, right and left, and Hudhaifi said: Whom does God want to make? His sustenance is in his voice: he did it."
"2195","(2195) Gandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He said about the muezzin: He joins his feet and faces the Qiblah, so when he says: The prayer has begun, he says with his face. To his right and to his left."
"2196","(2196) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Aoun bin Abi Juhayfy, on the authority of his father; Bilal ground the goat, then called the adhan, and put his fingers in its ears."
"2197","(2197) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: When the muezzin gives the call to prayer, he faces the qiblah. And he put his two fingers in her ears."
"2198","(2198) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Nasir, who said: I saw Ibn Umar giving the call to prayer to his camel. Sufyan said: I said: To him: Did you see him putting his two fingers in his ears? He said: No."
"2199","(2199) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: The call to prayer used to say: God is great, God is great. Akbar, then he puts his two fingers in his ears, and the first one to leave one of his fingers in his ears was Ibn al-Asam."
"2200","(2200) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; When he gave the call to prayer, he would face the qiblah and send out his hand, and when it was delivered, he would greet the prayer, greet the farmer, enter. Her fingers are in her ears."
"2201","(2201) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in him giving the call to prayer other than ablution, then descending. So he performs ablution."
"2202","(2202) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in giving the call to prayer on someone other than Ablution"
"2203","(2203) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders; He did not see any harm in a man calling the call to prayer without performing ablution, so if he wanted to stand up, he would perform ablution."
"2204","(2204) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad; He used to give the call to prayer without performing ablution."
"2205","(2205) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in someone who is not clean being called to prayer, and performing the prayer. And He is pure."
"2206","(2206) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Uthman, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’; He did not see any harm in saying the call to prayer without ablution."
"2207","(2207) Harami bin Amara bin Abi Hafsiya told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abdul Khaliq, on the authority of Hammad; He did not see any harm in a man saying the call to prayer without performing ablution."
"2208","(2208) Omar bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Abu Hurairah said: The muezzin does not give the call to prayer except Ablution"
"2209","(2209) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Maqil bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ata’; He disliked for a man to call the call to prayer without having performed ablution."
"2210","(2210) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Thuwayr, who said: I was a muezzin, so Mujahid ordered me not to give the call to prayer until I perform ablution."
"2211","(2211) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Talha, on the authority of Abu Sakhrah Jami’ bin Shaddad, on the authority of Musa bin Abdullah bin Yazid That Sulaiman bin Surad had companions who used to give the call to prayer in the army, and he used to order his servants to perform the pilgrimage. His call to prayer"
"2212","(2212) Ibn Aliyah told us, he said: I asked Yunus about speaking about the call to prayer and the iqamah? He said: Ubaidullah bin Ghallab told me, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He did not see any harm in that."
"2213","(2213) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan (h) and Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’: They did not see any harm in The muezzin speaks during his call to prayer."
"2214","(2214) Abbad told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Arouba, who said: He was his leader. He did not see any harm in that, and perhaps he did it. So he spoke in his call to prayer."
"2215","(2215) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’; He did not see any harm in the muezzin speaking during his call to prayer, nor between the call to prayer and the iqama."
"2216","(2216) Zaid bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah; That his father used to speak during his call to prayer."
"2217","(2217) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Amir al-Muzani, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, They both hated to speak until they had finished."
"2218","(2218) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad; He hated speaking during the call to prayer."
"2219","(2219) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail Al-Azraq, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; He disliked speaking during the call to prayer."
"2220","(2220) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated for the muezzin to speak in his call to prayer, until he finished."
"2221","(2221) Hammad bin Maqil told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Rawwad, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: I heard him say: When he spoke about... If it stays, it will be a feast."
"2222","(2222) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated to speak about the call to prayer and the iqamah until he had finished."
"2223","(2223) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: There is no harm in him."
"2224","(2224) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm for a man to speak during his iqama."
"2225","(2225) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Nasir, who said: I saw Ibn Umar giving the call to prayer for his camel."
"2226","(2226) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali al-Sulami, who said: I saw Rabi`i bin Harash giving the call to prayer on Bardhun."
"2227","(2227) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He saw no harm in a man calling the call to prayer and standing on his mount, then dismounting and praying."
"2228","(2228) Abdullah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He used to give the call to prayer on the camel, and he would dismount and perform it."
"2229","(2229) Hammad bin Khalid Al-Khayyat narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amri, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Al-Mujabir, who said: I saw Salim getting up. On the mount of the saddle and he gives the call to prayer."
"2230","(2230) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak al-Hinai, on the authority of al-Hasan al-Abdi, he said: I saw Abu Zayd, The companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his leg was injured in the cause of God. He was giving the call to prayer while sitting."
"2231","(2231) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: They hated for a man to call the call to prayer while he was sitting."
"2232","(2232) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; He disliked giving the call to prayer while sitting, unless there was an excuse."
"2233","(2233) Omar bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I said to him: Does a man give the call to prayer while sitting? He said: No, except from an illness. I said: Is it from drowsiness or laziness? He said: No."
"2234","(2234) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Shaddad, the client of Iyad bin Amir, on the authority of Bilal; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not give the call to prayer until you see dawn, like this, and he extended his hand. (Abu Dawud 535. Tabarani 1121)"
"2235","(2235) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Suwaid, on the authority of Bilal, who said: He would not give the call to prayer until he broke his throat. Fajr"
"2236","(2236) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Abu Mahdhuriya; He gave the call to prayer to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and to Abu Bakr and Omar, but he did not give the call to prayer until dawn came."
"2237","(2237) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: They did not give the call to prayer. Until dawn breaks."
"2238","(2238) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Ali, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: We accompanied Alqamiya to Mecca, so we left. At night, he heard a muezzin calling the call to prayer, and he said: This has violated the Sunnah of the Companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, if only he had When he was asleep, it was the last time for him, so when dawn came he called the call to prayer."
"2239","(2239) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sulaiman, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, on the authority of Fudayl bin Amr, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated to give the call to prayer before dawn."
"2240","(2240) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he said: I said to Nafi’: They used to call out before dawn? He said: The call only came at dawn."
"2241","(2241) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: They doubted the coming of dawn during the reign of Ibn Abbas, so he ordered He called the muezzin and established the prayer."
"2242","(2242) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Ibn Salem, on the authority of Amir, who said: He does not give the call to prayer until Its time enters."
"2243","(2243) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad, who said: When the muezzin gives the call to prayer, he faces the qiblah."
"2244","(2244) Gandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He said about the muezzin: He should join his legs and face the Qiblah."
"2245","(2245) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The muezzin faces the first The call to prayer, the shahada, and the iqamah: the direction of prayer."
"2246","(2246) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad; They liked it when the muezzin gave the call to face the qiblah."
"2247","(2247) Malik bin Ismail told us, he said: Zuhair told us, he said: Abu Matar al-Ja’fi told us, he said: I gave the adhan several times. Then Suwayd said to me: When you announce the call to prayer, face the Qiblah, for it is part of the Sunnah."
"2248","(2248) Marhum bin Abdul Aziz narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, the muezzin of the Holy House, who said: Omar came to us. Ibn Al-Khattab, and he said: When you call for prayer, then leave, and when you call for prayer, then wear your shoes."
"2249","(2249) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Othman, on the authority of Abu Jafar; That Ibn Omar used to recite the call to prayer and recite the Iqamah."
"2250","(2250) Abu Asama and Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of al-Hasan, and Muhammad, who said: It was It is astonishing for them that when the muezzin begins the Iqama, he proceeds and does not leave behind."
"2251","(2251) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He was deleting the Iqama."
"2252","(2252) Malik told us, he said: Ja’far al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He recites in the call to prayer, and follows Residence one after the other."
"2253","(2253) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father, and Muslim bin Abi Maryam; That Ali bin Hussein used to give the call to prayer, and when he reached it: Hail Ali al-Falah, he would say: Hail Ali the best of deeds, and he would say: It is the call to prayer. The first"
"2254","(2254) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to say in his call to prayer: Prayer is better than sleep, and perhaps he said: Hail to the best of deeds."
"2255","(2255) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: Ibn Umar may have added in his adhan: Hayy On the best of deeds."
"2256","(2256) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, who said: I saw Abu Mahdhuriya, who came and... A man called the call to prayer, so he called the call to prayer and stayed."
"2257","(2257) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of a sheikh from the people of Medina, on the authority of some of the sons of the Prophet’s muezzin. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: Ibn Umm Maktum used to give the call to prayer, and Bilal would perform the iqaamah. Perhaps Bilal would call the call to prayer, and Ibn Umm would perform the iqaamah. Muffled \n(Ibn Saad 207)"
"2258","(2258) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in a man calling the call to prayer, and someone else calling in prayer."
"2259","(2259) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Fazari, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: : Only the one who gives permission is in charge."
"2260","(2260) Ali told us, he said: Al-Ifriqi told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Nu’aym Al-Hadrami, on the authority of Ziyad bin Al-Harith. Al-Suda'i, he said: I was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and he commanded me, so I announced the call to prayer, and Bilal wanted to perform the prayer, so he said The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Indeed, Sadda’s brother called the call to prayer, and whoever calls the call to prayer should perform the prayer, so I stayed. (Abu Dawud 515, Tirmidhi 199)"
"2261","(2261) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Khalid, who said: When Ibn Umar gave the call to prayer, he would sit until he touched his seat. Earth"
"2262","(2262) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, he said: The companions of Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said that Bilal called the call to prayer twice, said the iqama twice, and sat while sitting."
"2263","(2263) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour bin Abi Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He sits The muezzin in Maghrib between the call to prayer and the iqamah."
"2264","(2264) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; Ibn Umm Maktum used to give the call to prayer while he was blind.\n(Muslim 287. Abu Dawud 536)"
"2265","(2265) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father; Ibn Umm Maktum used to give the call to prayer to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was blind."
"2266","(2266) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Wasil al-Ahdab, on the authority of Qubaysa bin Burmah, who said: I heard Ibn Masoud, He says: I do not like your muezzins to be your blind ones. He said: I thought he said it, nor do your reciters."
"2267","(2267) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Uqba, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He hated the blind man’s residence."
"2268","(2268) Abdul-Wahhab bin Ata’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of Malik bin Dinar, on the authority of Abi Aroub. Ibn al-Zubayr disliked the muezzin calling the call to prayer while he was blind."
"2269","(2269) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: It was for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Two muezzins: Bilal and Ibn Umm Maktum. (Muslim 2871 Darami 1191)"
"2270","(2270) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Mansour, who said: Abraham’s muezzin was blind."
"2271","(2271) Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of my nephew al-Zuhri, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jubayr; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not call to prayer during travel except by iqamah, except during prayer. In the morning, he used to give the call to prayer and give the prayer."
"2272","(2272) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’; Ibn Umar used to perform the iqaamah while travelling, except during the dawn prayer, when he used to give the call to prayer and perform the iqaamah."
"2273","(2273) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, on the authority of Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, he said: I came The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and with me was a cousin of mine, and he said: When you travel, give the call to prayer and stay, and let the elder of you lead the prayer.\n(Bukhari 628 and Muslim 293)"
"2274","(2274) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: They were commanded while traveling to give the call to prayer. And they will be established, and the most knowledgeable of them will lead them in prayer."
"2275","(2275) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Iqama is sufficient, except at dawn, for they They used to say: He gives the call to prayer and gives the call to prayer."
"2276","(2276) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: Urwah said: If you are on a journey, give the adhan. And stand, and if you wish, stand and do not call to prayer."
"2277","(2277) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: Iqama is sufficient."
"2278","(2278) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If you are in In your home, or on your journey, the Iqama is sufficient for you, and if you wish, you may pronounce the call to prayer, provided that you do not leave the Iqama to be repeated."
"2279","(2279) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; He was asked about travelers giving the call to prayer and saying the iqama? He said: The Iqama is sufficient for them, unless they are dispersed, and he wants to gather them together and give the call to prayer and perform the prayer."
"2280","(2280) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Zayd bin Jabir, who said: I stayed with an alcoholic in Dabiq for fifteen years. He did not add to the iqamah or call to prayer."
"2281","(2281) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Maimoon ibn Mihran, who said: When a people gathers on a journey, Their house was all together, so the residence is sufficient for them."
"2282","(2282) Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Harith, on the authority of his father, he said: We were with Abu Musa, With a spring of dates in Dar Al-Barid, so he called the call to prayer and said the iqama, so we said to him: What if you went out to the wilderness? He said: That and that are the same."
"2283","(2283) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who forgot the iqama while traveling, he said: That is sufficient."
"2284","(2284) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a traveler who forgot and prayed without the call to prayer or iqamah, he said: That is sufficient, and he used to say the same thing about a resident."
"2285","(2285) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he forgets the iqama while traveling, it is sufficient."
"2286","(2286) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha’i, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If you were on a journey and did not give the call to prayer and did not stand, So repeat the prayer."
"2287","(2287) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If he forgets the iqama while traveling, he repeats it."
"2288","(2288) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah (h) and on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who forgot the Iqama, he said: He is going to celebrate Eid."
"2289","(2289) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no prayer except by the iqamah."
"2290","(2290) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, who said: Ali said: Whatever man goes out to... The land of a poor man, and the time for prayer has come, so let him choose the best and cleanest spot, for every spot loves that God be remembered. In it, if he wishes, he may call the call to prayer and perform the iqama, and if he wishes, he may perform the iqama once and pray."
"2291","(2291) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Salman, who said: There will not be a man in the land of Qayyim. Then he performs ablution, and if he does not find water, he performs tayammum, then he calls for prayer, then performs it, except for one of the soldiers of God who is unseen. Tarafa\n(Bayhaqi 406. Abdul Razzaq 1955)"
"2292","(2292) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abu Harun al-Ghanawi, he said: Abu Uthman told us, he said: Salman said: It was not. A man in the land of Qayyah, then he called the call to prayer and said the iqama, except that one of God’s creation prayed behind him that no end of it can see."
"2293","(2293) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to say: Concerning a man who prays alone: he gives the call to prayer and performs the prayer.\n Ibn Sirin said: On the authority of a man who was a jurist: He used to perform qimam and did not give the call to prayer except in the morning prayer, for he gave the call to prayer during it. And He evaluates."
"2294","(2294) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to see when he prayed in Egypt alone, The Iqama is sufficient for it, except at dawn, for it is when he announces the call to prayer and performs the prayer.\n He said: Ibn Sirin used to say the same thing."
"2295","(2295) Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Ata’; That a man said to him: If I am alone, should I call the call to prayer and perform the iqaamah? He said: Yes."
"2296","(2296) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: I asked him if I was alone on me. Adhan? He said: Yes, call to prayer and stay."
"2297","(2297) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: My father used to give the call to prayer for himself and give prayers to him."
"2298","(2298) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Asim Al-Thaqafi, he said: Ata’ told us, he said: I entered with Ali bin Al-Hussein Ali Jabir. Ibn Abdullah, he said: The time for prayer came, so he called the call to prayer and performed the iqama."
"2299","(2299) Azhar Al-Samman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad used to pray in his house while the people remained."
"2300","(2300) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of Maimun, who said: If a man prays in his house, it is sufficient for him. Residence"
"2301","(2301) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who prays in his house without standing. He said: If he stays in prayer, that is better, but if he does not, that is sufficient."
"2302","(2302) Shababi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: We have been informed that men from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, when one of them prayed in his house, he would pronounce the first call to prayer, and the Iqama in every prayer."
"2303","(2303) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, and Alqamah, they said: We came to Abdullah in He went home and said: Did these people pray behind you? We said: No. He said: So stand up and pray, but he did not order the call to prayer or the iqamah.\n(Muslim 378, An-Nasa’i 618)"
"2304","(2304) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Waqid, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He did not live in a land where prayers were performed."
"2305","(2305) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Salma Abi Bishr, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: If you pray in your house The living muezzin rewarded you."
"2306","(2306) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If you are in Egypt, your stay in them is sufficient for you."
"2307","(2307) Abu Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Residence in Egypt is sufficient."
"2308","(2308) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Dalham bin Salih, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on a journey, and he heard a muezzin performing the iqama and led his companions in prayer."
"2309","(2309) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Aswad; That his father prayed in his house due to the excuse of having people stay there."
"2310","(2310) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If you hear the Iqamah while you are in Your house is sufficient for you if you wish."
"2311","(2311) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mundhir bin Tha’labiyah, who said: I asked Abu Majliz and said: I am in a village being established. What about praying in congregation? If I pray alone, will I give the call to prayer and perform the iqaamah? He said: If you wish, the public call to prayer is sufficient for you, and if you wish, then give the call to prayer and perform the iqama."
"2312","(2312) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Al-Ja’d Abu Uthman, on the authority of Anas; He entered the mosque and they had prayed, so he ordered a man to call to prayer and perform the iqama."
"2313","(2313) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, ‘Ata’, and Mujahid who said: If you enter a mosque and have been praying in it Prayer, or you do not stand up, stand up and then pray."
"2314","(2314) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: He gives the call to prayer and establishes prayer."
"2315","(2315) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sulaym, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; Concerning the people going to the mosque and he had prayed in it, he said: They call the call to prayer and perform the iqaamah, and he said: His leader: No one will come to you. Bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah."
"2316","(2316) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila; A man asked: I entered the mosque and its people were praying, should I give the call to prayer? He said: That is sufficient."
"2317","(2317) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who goes to the mosque and has prayed there, he said: He does not give the call to prayer or perform the prayer."
"2318","(2318) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazeed, who said: I entered a warrior’s mosque with Abraham, and he believed him but did not give the call to prayer. And he did not stand up."
"2319","(2319) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah; A man came to the mosque and they had prayed, so he went to perform the prayer, and Urwah said to him: Stop, for we have performed the prayer."
"2320","(2320) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, Mujahid, and Ikrimah, who said: If he enters the mosque and has He prayed in it, but he did not call to prayer or say the iqaamah."
"2321","(2321) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Bilal called the call to prayer at night, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded him to do so. He was permitted to call out: The servant slept. Then he came back and called out: The servant slept, and he said: \nI wish Bilal had not been born to his mother!\nAnd his forehead was wet with blood oozing out.\nHe said: And we learned that he commanded him to repeat the call to prayer. (Dar Qatni 54.55)"
"2322","(2322) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawwad, on the authority of Nafi’; It was said that Omar’s muezzin called the call to prayer before dawn, so Omar ordered him to repeat it."
"2323","(2323) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: When Al-Hassan was mentioned in his presence, those who call to prayer were At night, he said: they are empty and they cannot pray except by standing. If Omar ibn al-Khattab had overtaken them, he would have beaten them or caused pain. Their heads"
"2324","(2324) Muhammad bin Bishr and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; That the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had two muezzins who called the call to prayer. Ibn Numayr added to it: Ibn Umm Maktum. And Bilal."
"2325","(2325) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib ibn Yazid, the son of Nimr’s sister, who said: What The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had except one muezzin. He called the call to prayer when he sat on the pulpit and stood up when he descended. Then Abu Early in the same manner, then Omar in the same manner, until Othman arrived, and the people dispersed and multiplied, the third call was added at noon, or Al-Zora'a (Bukhari 912, Abu Dawud 1080)"
"2326","(2326) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad Ibn Sirin, who said: Women are not required to call the call to prayer, nor Residence"
"2327","(2327) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Women are not required to call the call to prayer or to perform the iqāmah."
"2328","(2328) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab And Al-Hasan said: Women are not required to call the call to prayer or to perform the Iqamah."
"2329","(2329) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: Women are not required to call the call to prayer, nor to perform the iqama."
"2330","(2330) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, similar to that."
"2331","(2331) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father, he said: We used to ask people: Do women have to call the call to prayer and perform the iqama? He said: No, and if they do it, then it is a remembrance."
"2332","(2332) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh, on the authority of a woman from the people of Mecca, who said: I said to Jabir bin Zaid: Is he staying? He said: No."
"2333","(2333) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Women are not required to call the call to prayer or to perform the iqama."
"2334","(2334) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ali, who said: Do not give the call to prayer, and do not perform the prayer."
"2335","(2335) Harami bin Amara told us, on the authority of Ghalib bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: Women are not required to call the call to prayer or to perform the iqama."
"2336","(2336) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Aisha, that she used to give the call to prayer and perform the prayer."
"2337","(2337) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha; Like him"
"2338","(2338) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Wahhab ibn Kaysan, who said: Ibn Umar was asked, Do women have to call the call to prayer? He became angry and said: I am forbidden from mentioning Allah."
"2339","(2339) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hafsa, who said: She used to perform the prayer when she prayed."
"2340","(2340) Yahya bin Ali Al-Aslami and Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: It is not On women’s residence."
"2341","(2341) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’ and Tawoos; Aisha used to give the call to prayer and perform the prayer."
"2342","(2342) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Salem, who said: If there is an issue, He will announce to you."
"2343","(2343) Malik bin Ismail told us, he said: Huraim told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: You evaluate The woman if she wants."
"2344","(2344) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered Bilal to give the call to prayer. On the Day of Conquest, above the Kaaba. (Abdul Razzaq 19444)"
"2345","(2345) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, who said: Among the Sunnah is the call to prayer in the minaret. And staying in the mosque, and Abdullah used to do that."
"2346","(2346) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: I asked about a man who wanted to give the call to prayer and stayed. He said: He celebrates Eid, and Sufyan said: He makes it an adhan and a prayer."
"2347","(2347) Al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Kudayna, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If he wanted to He called the call to prayer, and he stayed, saying: He will return."
"2348","(2348) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of a statement, on the authority of Qais, who said: Omar said: If I had pronounced the call to prayer with the Caliph, I would have given him the call to prayer."
"2349","(2349) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Dirar, on the authority of Zazan, who said: If people knew what is in the virtue of the call to prayer, they would be disturbed over it. With swords."
"2350","(2350) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Saad, who said: Because someone who is stronger in reciting the call to prayer is more beloved to me than performing Hajj. I perform Umrah and I strive hard."
"2351","(2351) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ka'b said: Whoever calls the call to prayer, seventy good deeds are recorded for him, and if he stays in prayer, that is better."
"2352","(2352) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abbad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O God, guide the imams and forgive the muezzins. (Abdul Razzaq 1839 and Ahmed 419)"
"2353","(2353) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Yahya, who said: It was narrated that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: If people knew what is in the call to prayer, they would agree with it. He said: And it was said: Hasten to the call to prayer, but do not hasten to say the Iqamah. (Ahmed 29)"
"2354","(2354) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The muezzin, the muhtasib, is the first to be clothed."
"2355","(2355) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Talha bin Yahya, he said: I heard Issa bin Talha, he said: I heard Muawiyah says: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: The muezzins will have the longest necks on the Day of Resurrection.\n(Muslim 290. Ibn Majah 725)"
"2356","(2356) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The people of righteousness and good people are among The muezzins, the first to be clothed on the Day of Resurrection."
"2357","(2357) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: A sheikh from the people of Basra told us, he said: Al-Qasim bin Awf told us Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Bilal will be the master of the muezzins on the Day of Resurrection, and no Only a believer follows him, and the muezzins will have the longest necks on the Day of Resurrection. (Tabarani 5118)"
"2358","(2358) Yazeed narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Subayh, he said: Abu Fatima narrated to us, a man who met the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Ibn Masoud said: If I were the muezzin, I would not mind not performing the Hajj, nor going on a campaign."
"2359","(2359) Yazid and Waki’ told us, they said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Shubail bin Awf, he said: Omar said: Who are your muezzins? They said: Our slaves and our masters. He said: This is a great deficiency in you. However, Waki` said: a lot, or a great deal."
"2360","(2360) Yazid and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, who said: Qais said: Omar said: If only I could bear the call to prayer with the Caliph I would have given permission."
"2361","(2361) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn al-Walid, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Ubaid ibn Umair, on the authority of Aisha, she said: : I do not see that these verses were revealed except regarding the muezzins: {And who is better in speech than he who invites to Allah and does righteousness and says, “Indeed, I am of Muslims}"
"2362","(2362) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn al-Walid, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Nafi’, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I do not see These verses were revealed except regarding the muezzins: {And who is better in speech than he who invites to Allah and does righteousness, and says, ‘Indeed, I am of the Muslims’}."
"2363","(2363) Abu Asama told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Al-Hakam told me, he said: Yahya bin Abbad Abu Hubira told me. On the authority of Sheikh, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The muezzin will be forgiven for raising his voice. And every wet and dry thing confirms it. (Ahmad 2/411)"
"2364","(2364) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abu Al-Anbas Sa’id bin Kathir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Raise your voice with the call to prayer, for it bears witness to everything you heard."
"2365","(2365) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The muezzin bears witness to everything, wet and dry. He heard you"
"2366","(2366) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubair bin Adiy, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He said to a man: What is your business? He said: The call to prayer. He said: What an excellent deed your deed is, and everything that you hear bears witness to you."
"2367","(2367) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Alqamiya and Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla came out to Bedouins of theirs. Ibrahim said: I was amazed that Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla used to appoint a son of his as a servant. He gives the call to prayer."
"2368","(2368) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in a boy giving the call to prayer before he He has a wet dream."
"2369","(2369) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail al-Azraq, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, who said: There is no harm for a boy to give the call to prayer if he does the call to prayer well before saying the call to prayer. To have a wet dream."
"2370","(2370) Ismail Ibn Ali and Yazid Ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawwi, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Abi Many, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Issa ibn Talha, who said: We entered upon Muawiyah, and the muezzin came and gave the call to prayer, and he said: Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest. Then Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan said the same thing, and he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. Mu'awiyah said something like that, and he said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. Mu`awiyah said something like that, then he said: Thus I heard your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say. (Ahmad 4/91, Darmi 1202)"
"2371","(2371) Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Ayyub, who said: Ka’b bin Alqamih narrated to me, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If you hear the muezzin, say As he says (Muslim 2888, Abu Dawud 524)"
"2372","(2372) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yazid, on the authority of Abu Sa’id The numb one; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say something like what the muezzin says. (Abu Dawud 525. Ibn Majah 720)"
"2373","(2373) He told us about his youth, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Abu al-Malih, on the authority of Umm Habiba. (Ahmad 326. An-Nasa’i 9865)"
"2374","(2374) (H) Affan told us, he said: Abu Awani told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, on the authority of Abdullah bin Utba, on the authority of Umm Habib, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; When he heard the muezzin, he would say as he said until he remained silent."
"2375","(2375) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Al Harith, on the authority of His father; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say something like what the muezzin says, so when he reached the message, he greeted the prayer, hailed the Al-Falah said: There is no power nor strength except with Allah. (Tabarani 3266)"
"2376","(2376) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Ali; When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard the voice of the caller saying: I bear witness that there is no god but God, he would say: And I. He said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. He said: And I am."
"2377","(2377) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard the muezzin, he would say: And I, and I."
"2378","(2378) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of someone who informed him, on the authority of Mujahid; That when the muezzin said: Hail to the Salat, he said: The one seeking help is Allah. Then, when he said: Hail to the Falah, he said: There is neither power nor power. Your strength is only in Allah."
"2379","(2379) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Whoever says like what the muezzin says will have Similar to his reward."
"2380","(2380) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: When you hear the muezzin, say as he says, and when he says : Come to the prayer, so say: There is no power nor strength except with Allah. Then when he says: The prayer has begun, then say: Oh God, Lord of this. The complete supplication, and the established prayer, give Muhammad his request on the Day of Resurrection, for no man will say it when he rises except May God include him in the intercession of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the Day of Resurrection."
"2381","(2381) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders; When Othman heard the muezzin giving the call to prayer, he would say just as he used to say in all the tashahhud and takbeer, then he would say: Hail Ali. Prayer. He said: Whatever God wills, and there is no power nor strength except in God. And when he said: The prayer has begun, he said: Welcome to those who say Just and truthful, and in prayer, welcome and welcome, then he gets up to pray."
"2382","(2382) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, who said: It is rude to hear the muezzin. He says: There is no god but Allah, and Allah is the greatest, and then you do not answer him."
"2383","(2383) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Musayyab ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: It is unfair to You hear the call to prayer, then do not say what he says."
"2384","(2384) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas, who said: The last covenant made by the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace if he appoints a muezzin who does not take any reward for his call to prayer. (Tirmidhi 209. Abu Dawud 532)"
"2385","(2385) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; He disliked the muezzin taking a slur over his call to prayer and saying: If it was given without asking, then there is no problem."
"2386","(2386) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Aoun ibn Musa, on the authority of Mu’awiyah ibn Qurayh, who said: It used to be said: He does not give you permission except Accountable"
"2387","(2387) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Amara bin Zazan, on the authority of Yahya al-Baka’, who said: I was holding Ibn Umar’s hand while he was He was circumambulating the Kaaba, and a man from among the muezzins of the Kaaba met him and said: Indeed, I love you for the sake of God. Then Ibn Umar said: Indeed, I hate you. For God's sake, you improve your voice to take dirhams."
"2388","(2388) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The muezzin called the call to prayer. Satan fled until he was accompanied by spirits, which was thirty miles from Medina. (Muslim 15)"
"2389","(2389) Muhammad bin Musab told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: When the muezzin calls for prayer, Satan will turn away and have a fart, and when he has finished, he will catch you. So when he dresses with it, he turns away. (Muslim 398. Ahmad 2/522)"
"2390","(2390) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Omar bin Saeed bin Abi Hussein Al-Makki; A muezzin gave the call to prayer, and he rejoiced in his call to prayer, so Omar bin Abdul Aziz said to him: Give the call to prayer with tolerance, otherwise we will isolate ourselves."
"2391","(2391) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hallam ibn Salih, on the authority of Faid ibn Bukair, on the authority of Hudhayf, who said: Whoever, God willing, He places his sustenance in the sound of his actions."
"2392","(2392) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The call to prayer is decisive."
"2393","(2393) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The key to prayer is purity, its prohibition is takbir and its permissibility is the salutation (Dharmi). 687)"
"2394","(2394) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, he said: Abdullah said: Prayer is forbidden. Takbir, and its analysis is salutation."
"2395","(2395) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sufyan Al-Saadi, on the authority of Abu Nadhra, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The key to prayer is purity, its prohibition is takbeer, and its permissibility is the salutation."
"2396","(2396) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Kurayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The key to prayer. The birds, their prohibition of the takbeer, and their permissibility of the salutation."
"2397","(2397) Ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Badeel, on the authority of Abu al-Jawzai, on the authority of Aisha, she said: It was The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would begin the prayer with the takbir, and he would end it with the salutation. (Muslim 640 and Abu Dawud 779)"
"2398","(2398) Ibn Fudayl and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Uthman al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Salem, who said: Abu al-Darda’ said: For every Something is a slogan, and the slogan of prayer is the takbir."
"2399","(2399) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, and Tawus, who said: The tashahud is the completion of the prayer, and the salutation is then Her judgment"
"2400","(2400) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Waqa’i, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, who said: There is no prayer after the salutation."
"2401","(2401) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: When the imam greets, then those behind him have departed."
"2402","(2402) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Yazid, he said: I saw Omar Ibn al-Khattab opened the prayer and said the takbir, then he said: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, and Blessed be Your Name, and exalted is Your Grandfather, and there is no god. Other than you"
"2403","(2403) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When Omar began the prayer, he said “Allahu Akbar,” and he mentioned an example Hadith of Husayn, and he added to it: He speaks out loud. He said: And he said: Abraham did not say them out loud."
"2404","(2404) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: I heard Omar say when he opened the prayer: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, and Blessed be Your name and exalted is Your glory, and there is no god but You."
"2405","(2405) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah; He went to Omar, and they said to him: Preserve for us what you can. When he came, he said: From what you have memorized, he performed ablution twice and scattered Twice, when he said the takbir, or when he stood up to pray, he said: Glory be to You, O God, and praise be to You, and Blessed be Your Name and exalted is Your Grandfather, and do not God other than you"
"2406","(2406) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah; When he opened the prayer, he would say: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, and Blessed be Your name, and exalted is Your glory, and there is no god but You."
"2407","(2407) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Hakim bin Jabir; When Omar opened the prayer, he would say: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, and Blessed be Your name, and exalted is Your glory, and there is no god but You."
"2408","(2408) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, he said: I was informed that Abu Bakr used to say something like that."
"2409","(2409) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wael, who said: When Omar began the prayer, he said: Glory be to You. Oh God, and with your praise, and blessed be your name and exalted be your glory, and there is no god but you, who can hear us."
"2410","(2410) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Omar; When he began the prayer, he said: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, and Blessed be Your Name and exalted be Your Grandfather, and there is no god but You."
"2411","(2411) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Abbad ibn Asim, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he opened the prayer, he said: God is Great, three times, praise. To God a lot, three times, Glory be to God, morning and evening, three times, O God, I seek refuge in You from the accursed Satan, from hamzah, naffhah, nafthhih. (Bayhaqi 35)"
"2412","(2412) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Ammar ibn Asim, on the authority of Ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, on the authority of his father, said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying the Duha prayer, and he mentioned something like the hadith of Ibn Idris."
"2413","(2413) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Talha bin Yazid Al-Ansari. On the authority of Hudhayf, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stood up one night during Ramadan in a tree made of palm leaves, then He poured a bucket of water on him, then said: God is the Greatest, the Possessor of kingdom, might, pride, and greatness.\n(Ahmad 5/4000 An-Nasa’i 1378)"
"2414","(2414) Suwayd bin Amr Al-Kalbi told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Abi Salamah told us, he said: Al-Majshun informed us My uncle, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Ali, who said: Whenever the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, opened Prayer. He said, “Allahu Akbar,” then he said: “I turn my face toward the One who created the heavens and the earth, upright, and I am not of the polytheists. Indeed, my prayer My sacrifice, my life, and my death belong to God, Lord of the worlds, He has no partner, and with that I was commanded, and I am the first of the Muslims. Oh God, you are The King, there is no god but You, You are my Lord and I am Your servant. I wronged myself and confessed my sin, so forgive me all my sins. No one can forgive sins except You, and guide me to the best of morals. No one can guide me to the best except You, and turn away from them. No one can take away from me my bad except You. I am with You and I am pleased with You, and all goodness is in Your hands. I am with You. And to you, blessed and exalted, I seek your forgiveness and repent to you. (Muslim 2011, Tirmidhi 3421)"
"2415","(2415) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bai, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: I heard Amr ibn Maymun, he said: Omar led the morning prayer with us while he was travelling. With Dhul-Allāfī and he was going to Mecca, so he said: God is Great, Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, and Blessed be Your Name and Most High. Your grandfather, and there is no god but you."
"2416","(2416) Zaid bin Hubab narrated to us, saying: Ja’far bin Sulaiman Al-Dhabi narrated to me, on the authority of Ali bin Ali Al-Rifai’i, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to begin the prayer by saying: Glory be to You Oh God, and with your praise, and blessed be your name and exalted be your glory, and there is no god but you. (Ibn Majah 804. An-Nasa’i 973)"
"2417","(2417) Hushaym told us, he said: Juwaybir told us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak: In his saying: And glorify the praise of your Lord when you rise, He said: When you stand up for prayer, you say these words: Glory be to You, O God, and praise be to You, and Blessed be Your Name and Most High Your Grandfather, and do not God other than you"
"2418","(2418) Ibn Fudail and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, He said: Ibn Masoud said: One of the most beloved words to God is for a man to say: Glory be to You, O God, and praise be to You, and Blessed be Your Name and Most High. Your grandfather, and there is no god but You. My Lord, I have wronged myself, so forgive me my sins. Indeed, no one forgives sins except You."
"2419","(2419) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, who said: When Omar began the prayer, he would raise his voice. He hears us saying: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, and Blessed be Your name and exalted be Your glory, and there is no god but You."
"2420","(2420) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, he said: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Khalil, on the authority of Ali He said: I heard him when he said the greatest in the prayer. He said: There is no god but You, Glory be to You. Indeed, I have wronged myself, so forgive my sins. No one forgives sins except You."
"2421","(2421) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan and Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Ibn Abi Al-Khalil, on the authority of Ali, Like him"
"2422","(2422) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Haytham, who said: I heard Ibn Umar say when The prayer opens: God is great, great, and Glory be to God and praise be to Him early and in the evening. O God, make him the most beloved thing. To me, and I fear something about me."
"2423","(2423) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, and the like."
"2424","(2424) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, who said: I saw the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. When he begins the prayer, he raises his hand until it is in line with his shoulders. (Tirmidhi 256. Abu Dawud 721)"
"2425","(2425) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wa’il ibn Hajar, who said: I came to Medina, So I said: Let us look at the prayer of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Then he said “Allahu Akbar” and raised his hand until I saw his thumbs. Close to her ears. (Abu Daw9 728. Nasa’i 1191)"
"2426","(2426) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib, who said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he opened the prayer, raising his hands to the point that they were almost level with his ears. (Ahmad 4/202; Abd al-Razzaq 3530)"
"2427","(2427) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Nasr bin Asim, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Huwairith said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, raising his hands so that they were aligned with the branches of his ears. (Muslim 26. Abu Dawud 745)"
"2428","(2428) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad; Omar used to raise his hands in prayer, following the example of his shoulders."
"2429","(2429) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to raise his hands as high as his shoulders."
"2430","(2430) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Do not let the hands go beyond the ears in prayer."
"2431","(2431) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: He does not go beyond his ears with his hand. The opening"
"2432","(2432) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad; He used to raise his hands as high as his shoulders."
"2433","(2433) Ishaq bin Mansour and Ubaid Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Misra, he said: When our companions opened the prayer, they would raise their hands to their ears."
"2434","(2434) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulaiman, on the authority of Ata’. He said: Do not exceed with your hands. I hear you in supplications or something else."
"2435","(2435) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of Muharib, who said: If you saw Abdullah ibn Umar when he stood up for prayer... He said: Thus, and raised his hand to match his face."
"2436","(2436) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to raise his hands at the same level as his shoulders."
"2437","(2437) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muhammad, on the authority of Al-Araj, who said: I heard Abu Hurairah say: Among you is he who says thus, and Sufyan raised his hands until it exceeded his head, and among you is he who says thus, And he placed his hands near his stomach, and among you is he who says like this, meaning: like his shoulders."
"2438","(2438) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Bakr, who said: I saw Salim, when he stood up, raise his hands like From his side"
"2439","(2439) Ahmad bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Salem; He used to raise his hands as high as his shoulders."
"2440","(2440) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, who said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, raises his hand when he opens the prayer, and when he bows and after he raises it, but he does not raise his hand in between. The two prostrations."
"2441","(2441) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wa’il ibn Hajar, he said: I saw the Prophet praying. May God bless him and grant him peace. He raises his hands every time he bows and raises himself."
"2442","(2442) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Nasr ibn Asim, on the authority of Malik ibn al-Hawrith, He said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying “Allahu Akbar” when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing until it was aligned with them. The branches of her ears."
"2443","(2443) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would raise his hands when he opened his prayers, when he bowed, and when he raised his head, but he did not It goes beyond our ears."
"2444","(2444) Hushaym told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Yasar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace; Like that"
"2445","(2445) Hushaym told us, he said: Laith told us, on the authority of Ata’, he said: I saw Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, Ibn Umar, and Ibn Abbas and Ibn Al-Zubayr; They raise their hands, like the hadith of Al-Zuhri."
"2446","(2446) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Hamza told us, he said: I saw Ibn Abbas raising his hand when he began the prayer. And when he bows, and when he raises his head from bowing."
"2447","(2447) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace May the peace and blessings of God be upon him in their prayers, as if their hands were fans when they bowed, and when they raised their heads."
"2448","(2448) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas; He used to raise his hand when he entered into prayer, when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing."
"2449","(2449) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to raise his hands when bowing and prostrating. (Ibn Majah 866. Daraqutni 11)"
"2450","(2450) Muadh bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, who said: Al-Hasan used to do it."
"2451","(2451) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad used to raise his hands when he entered the prayer, and when he bowed, and when he His head is from bowing."
"2452","(2452) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khaled; Abu Qalabab used to raise his hand when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing."
"2453","(2453) Hushaym told us, saying: Abdul Hamid bin Jafar Al-Ansari told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Ata’. Al-Qurashi, he said: I saw Abu Hamid Al-Sa’idi with ten of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: No Shall I tell you about the prayer of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? They said: Come. He said: I saw that when he said “Allahu Akbar” at the beginning of the prayer, he raised his hand, and when he bowed, he raised his hand, and when he When bowing, he raises his hands, then remains standing until every bone falls into place, then he descends, prostrating. And he grows up. (Tirmidhi 304, Abu Dawud 730)"
"2454","(2454) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of Muharib ibn Dathar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I saw him raising His hand while bowing and prostrating, so I said to him: What is this? He said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up for the two rak’ahs, he would say “Allahu Akbar” and raise his hands. (Bukhari 739, Abu Dawud 741)"
"2455","(2455) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Isa, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib; When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, began the prayer, he would raise his hands, and then he would not raise them until he finished.\n(Abu Dawud 749. Daraqutni 22)"
"2456","(2456) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Abd God said: Shall I not show you the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He did not raise his hand except once.\n(Tirmidhi 257 Abu Daw 748)"
"2457","(2457) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Qitaf al-Nashili, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of His father; That Ali used to raise his hands when he began the prayer, and then he would not return."
"2458","(2458) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah; He used to raise his hands at the beginning of the opening, and then he would not raise them."
"2459","(2459) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; He used to raise his hands at the beginning of the takbeer, and then he would not raise them."
"2460","(2460) Hushaym told us, saying: Husayn and Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham; He used to say: When you say the “Allahu Akbar” during the opening of the prayer, raise your hands, and then do not raise them during the rest of the prayer."
"2461","(2461) Waki` and Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: They were the companions of Abdullah, and the companions of Ali, they do not raise their hands except at the opening of the prayer. Waki’ said: Then they do not repeat it."
"2462","(2462) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Husayn and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Do not raise your hands in Nothing of the prayer except in the first opening."
"2463","(2463) Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Khaythami and Ibrahim, he said: They did not raise Their hands, except at the beginning of the prayer."
"2464","(2464) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ismail, who said: Qais used to raise his hands as soon as he entered. The prayer, then he does not raise it."
"2465","(2465) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The hands are raised in Seven situations: when he stands for prayer, when he sees the House, on al-Safa and al-Marwah, on Arafat, in a gathering, and at The stones"
"2466","(2466) Muawiyah bin Hashim narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muslim Al-Janni, who said: He was Ibn Abi Layla. He raises his hands first when he says “Allahu Akbar.”"
"2467","(2467) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I never saw Ibn Umar raise his hand except The first time it opens."
"2468","(2468) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Aswad and Al-Qamah; Indeed, they used to raise their hands when they opened, and then they would not return."
"2469","(2469) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Ayyash, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Abjar, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, said: I prayed with Omar, and he did not raise his hands during any of his prayers until he opened the prayer. He said Abd al-Malik: And I saw al-Sha’bi, Ibrahim, and Abu Ishaq not raising their hands except when they opened the battle. Prayer"
"2470","(2470) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, who said: He opened the life of the prayer, then he said “Allahu Akbar”, then he said: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, and Blessed be Your name and exalted is Your glory, and there is no god but You. I seek refuge in God from the accursed Satan, Praise To God, Lord of the worlds."
"2471","(2471) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: I heard Omar starting the prayer and saying “Allahu Akbar” and he said: : Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, Blessed be Your name and exalted is Your glory, and there is no god but You. Then he seeks refuge."
"2472","(2472) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to say: I seek refuge in God from the accursed Satan, or I seek refuge in God, the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing from the accursed Satan."
"2473","(2473) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Khams, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim bin Yassar, he said: My father and I heard him. I seek refuge in the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing. He said: What is this? Say: I seek refuge in God from Satan, the accursed. Indeed, God is the Hearer, the Knower."
"2474","(2474) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad; He used to seek refuge before and after reciting the Book and opening it, and he would say in his refuge: I seek refuge in God, the Hearer. The All-Knowing of the instigations of the devils, and I seek refuge in God lest they be present."
"2475","(2475) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Abbad ibn Asim, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, on the authority of his father, said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he opened the prayer, he said: O God, I seek refuge in You from Satan, the accursed, from his hamzah, his blowing, and his blowing."
"2476","(2476) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: When he says “Allahu Akbar,” or “Allahu Akbar,” or Allah is sufficient for it in the opening, and he prostrates the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"2477","(2477) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: If he glorifies God, or God, in the opening of Prayer is part of the takbeer."
"2478","(2478) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Abi Muslim, who said: I heard Abu Al-Aliyah being asked, “What was the matter?” Do the prophets open the prayer? He said: By monotheism, glorification, and praise."
"2479","(2479) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: With which of the names of God did the prayer begin, that is sufficient for you."
"2480","(2480) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If he forgets the opening takbeer He resumed."
"2481","(2481) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who forgets the opening takbeer, he said: The takbeer of bowing is sufficient."
"2482","(2482) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; He said: Concerning a man, if he forgets to say “Allahu Akbar” when he begins the prayer, then he should say “Allahu Akbar” when he mentions, and if he does not even say “Allahu Akbar.” He prays his prayer, and bowing is sufficient for it."
"2483","(2483) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Hammad, who said: If the imam forgets the first takbirah that begins With this prayer he repeated it. The ruling said: The takbeerah of bowing is sufficient."
"2484","(2484) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Bakr, who said: He says takbir when he mentions it."
"2485","(2485) Ismail bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh bin Zaitoun, who said: I saw Umm al-Darda’ raising her hand in the same way. On her shoulders when the prayer begins, and when the imam says, “God hears those who praise Him,” she raises her hands during the prayer and says: Oh God, our Lord, praise be to You."
"2486","(2486) Hushaym told us, he said: A sheikh of ours told us, he said: I heard Ata’; A woman was asked: How does she raise her hands during prayer? He said: Follow her breasts."
"2487","(2487) Rawad bin Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Her hands should be raised at the same level as her shoulders."
"2488","(2488) Khalid bin Hayyan told us, on the authority of Issa bin Kathir, on the authority of Hammad; He used to say in the mirror: When she begins the prayer, she should raise her hands to her breasts."
"2489","(2489) Muhammad bin ??kar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: The woman gestures with her hands to say “Allahu Akbar.” Like a man? He said: Do not raise her hands like a man, and he pointed and lowered his hands very low, and brought them together very close to him, and said: Indeed A woman has an appearance that a man does not have, and if she leaves that, there is no blame."
"2490","(2490) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, he said: Yahya bin Maimun told me, he said: Asim Al-Ahwal told me, he said: I saw Hafsiya bint Sirin said the takbir during the prayer, and gestured following the example of her breasts, and Yahya described it and raised all of his hands."
"2491","(2491) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Alqamiya and Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abd God, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to say “Allahu Akbar” in every rising, positioning, standing, and sitting, and Abu Bakr, And Omar. (Tirmidhi 253. Ahmad 443)"
"2492","(2492) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Asam, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was And peace be upon him, Abu Bakr, Omar, and Othman do not diminish the takbeer. (Ahmad 3/1251 Abd al-Razzaq 250)"
"2493","(2493) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun; Omar used to say the takbeer completely."
"2494","(2494) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Nu’aym bin Hakim, on the authority of Abu Maryam, he said: Ammar said: If only Only the two times of takbeer are performed by Ali, meaning: when he bows, and when he prostrates."
"2495","(2495) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: Qais bin Abbad advised me to I say Akbar every time I prostrate and every time I rise."
"2496","(2496) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Wahhab bin Kaysan, who said: Jabir bin Abd was God teaches us to say “Allahu Akbar” in prayer. We say “Allahu Akbar” when we lower it, and when we raise it."
"2497","(2497) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ubad Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’; That Marwan used to succeed Abu Hurairah, so he used to recite the takbeer in full, and Ibn Umar used to perform the takbeer in full."
"2498","(2498) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah, who said: Ibn Masoud used to complete Takbeer"
"2499","(2499) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Razin, on the authority of Ali; He used to say “Allahu Akbar” every time he prostrated, every time he rose, and every time he got up."
"2500","(2500) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Razin, who said: I prayed behind Ali, And Ibn Masoud, they used to recite the takbir completely."
"2501","(2501) Hatem bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of alcohol; He used to say “Allahu Akbar” when he prostrated, and when he stood up between the two rak’ahs."
"2502","(2502) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu Uthman; He used to say “Allahu Akbar” when he prostrated, and when he stood up between the two rak’ahs."
"2503","(2503) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Amr ibn Muriya, on the authority of Ibrahim; He used to say “Allahu Akbar” completely."
"2504","(2504) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar; Ibn Al-Zubayr used to glorify Allah because of his revival."
"2505","(2505) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Dawud ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanam, On the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ash’ari; He said to his people: Stand up so that I may lead with you the prayer of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So we lined up behind him, so he said “Allahu Akbar.” Then he recited, then he said “Allahu Akbar,” then he bowed, then he raised his head and said “Allahu Akbar,” and he did that in all his prayers.\n(Ahmad 342. Tabarani 3411)"
"2506","(2506) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Burayd bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: He prayed. Ali’s prayer on the Day of Jamal. He reminded us of the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Either we will be We forgot it, or we left it intentionally. He says “Allahu Akbar” in every raising and lowering, standing and sitting, and he says salaam. Right and left\n(Ibn Majah 917. Ahmad 4/392)"
"2507","(2507) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Saeed narrated to us, he said: Al-Walid narrated to us, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Jarir, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir said: Imran bin Husayn and I prayed with Ali, and he began to say “Allahu Akbar” when he prostrated, and when he raised his head, When he finished his prayer, Imran said: This is what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed for us.\n(Bukhari 826. Muslim 33)"
"2508","(2508) Hafs told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, he said: Sa’id bin Jubayr used to say “Allahu Akbar” whenever he rose and whenever he bowed, he said: This was mentioned to Abu Ja`far, and he said: He knew that it was the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Sa’id said: It was only Something with which a man adorns his prayer."
"2509","(2509) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Ali bin Husayn informed me, he said: It was a prayer The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and it was mentioned to him that Abu Hurairah used to say “Allahu Akbar” with every lowering and raising. (Abdul Razzaq 2497)"
"2510","(2510) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: I saw Ali praying at the Maqam, saying “Allahu Akbar” In every setting and raising, he said: So I went to Ibn Abbas and told him about that, and Ibn Abbas said to me: Isn’t that a prayer? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has no mother for Ikrimah. (Bukhari 787. Ibn Khuzaymah 577)"
"2511","(2511) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; When he prayed for us, he would say “Allahu Akbar” whenever he raised and lowered it, and when he left, he would say: “I resemble your prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” May God bless him and grant him peace. (Bukhari 785. Muslim 293)"
"2512","(2512) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Sha`bi, on the authority of al-Hasan ibn Imran, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, said: I prayed behind the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, but he did not pronounce the takbeer completely. (Ahmad 3/407)"
"2513","(2513) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Imran; Omar bin Abdul Aziz did not recite the takbeer completely."
"2514","(2514) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, who said: I prayed behind Omar bin Abdul Aziz, but he did not complete it. Takbeer"
"2515","(2515) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The first person to decrease the takbeer was Ziyad."
"2516","(2516) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, who said: I prayed behind Al-Qasim and Salem, but they did not complete it. Takbeer"
"2517","(2517) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Al-Qasim and Salem; Like him"
"2518","(2518) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, who said: I prayed with Sa’id ibn Jubayr, but he did not perform the prayer. Takbeer"
"2519","(2519) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Yazid al-Faqir, who said: Ibn Umar used to lack the takbeer. Concerning prayer, Mas’ar said: If he lowers himself after bowing to prostrate, he does not say “Allahu Akbar,” and if he wants to prostrate the second time, he does not pronounce “Allahu Akbar.”"
"2520","(2520) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar and Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: When he overtakes you The man is standing in a bowing position, for a single takbeer is sufficient for him."
"2521","(2521) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Ismail, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah bin Al-Zubayr and Zayd bin Thabit ; They were both coming while the imam was bowing, so they would say “Allahu Akbar” at the opening of prayer and bowing."
"2522","(2522) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: One is sufficient for you."
"2523","(2523) Ibn Aliyah told us, he said: I said to Ibn Abi Najih: A man goes to the people while they are bowing and says “Allahu Akbar” Is it arrogant and he kneels? He said: Mujahid used to say: It is sufficient."
"2524","(2524) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Takbir is sufficient, but if it is more, that is better."
"2525","(2525) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, who said: Takbirah is sufficient."
"2526","(2526) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Amara, on the authority of Bakr, who said: I heard him say: “Allahu Akbar.”"
"2527","(2527) Khaled bin Hayyan told us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of Maimun; It is sufficient to enlarge it."
"2528","(2528) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to like to say “Allahu Akbar” twice, so if he was in a hurry or forgot to say “Allahu Akbar” then that is sufficient."
"2529","(2529) Wakī’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bā, he said: I asked the arbitrator, and he said: It is sufficient to say greatness."
"2530","(2530) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Amr bin Muhajir, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, he said: He says takbir. Takbiratini."
"2531","(2531) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Hanafi, who said: I asked Ibn Sirin about a man who comes To the imam while he is bowing? He said: To begin the prayer with “Allahu Akbar” and “Allahu Akbar” while bowing, but if he does not do that, then that is sufficient."
"2532","(2532) Ishaq bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, he said: He says “Allahu Akbar” for opening and “Allahu Akbar” for bowing."
"2533","(2533) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, he said: He says “Allahu Akbar.” Takbiratini."
"2534","(2534) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: If you come while the imam is bowing, and you place your hands On your knees before he raised his head, I had caught up with you."
"2535","(2535) Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, who said: Whoever catches the Imam Before he raised his head, he performed the prostration."
"2536","(2536) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: I said: A man goes to the people while they are bowing, and he has Did the imam raise his head? He said: Some of you are imams of others."
"2537","(2537) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Maimun, who said: If you enter the mosque and the people are bowing, then you say “Allahu Akbar.” Then you bowed before they raised their heads, so you had performed the bow before they raised their heads."
"2538","(2538) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Salem Al-Barrad, who said: We came to Abu Masoud and said: Show us his prayer. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said the takbir, then bowed, and placed his hands on his knees, then said: This is how he prayed. With us\n(Abu Dawud 859. Ahmad 4/119)"
"2539","(2539) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wa’il ibn Hajar, who said: I was among those who He came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: Let us look at the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. When he wanted to bow, he rose. His hands, then he bowed and placed his hands on his knees."
"2540","(2540) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Ali bin Yahya bin Khallad, on the authority of Rifa’i bin Rafi’; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a man: When you face the qiblah, say “Allahu Akbar” and recite whatever you want. You kneel, so put your palms on your knees, and make your bowing straight. (Tirmidhi 302 and Ahmad 340)"
"2541","(2541) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Haritha, on the authority of Amrah, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; He bowed and placed his hands on his knees. (Ibn Majah 874)"
"2542","(2542) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, who said: I saw Omar kneeling and he placed his hands on His knees"
"2543","(2543) Ibn Fudail and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Omar; When he bowed, he would place his hands on his knees."
"2544","(2544) Abdi and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Zubair bin Adiy, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Sa’d, he said: I kneeled. Next to my father, I put my hands between my knees, and Saad hit my hand, then said: We used to do this, then we were ordered With knees\n(Bukhari 7901 Muslim 31)"
"2545","(2545) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Khaythāmī, who said: Whenever Ibn Umar bowed, he would place His hands are on his knees."
"2546","(2546) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: A man from among the companions of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was one of the Ansar on the Day of Qadisiyah, and he said: When he bows, let him place his hands on his knees. And let him rise until his tailbone rises."
"2547","(2547) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: When you kneel, keep your face straight. For the Qiblah, place your hands on your knees, and do not slaughter like a donkey."
"2548","(2548) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of Ali, who said: So When you kneel, place your palms on your knees, and spread your back, and do not bow your head, do not direct it, do not stretch out, and do not You get hold of it."
"2549","(2549) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, who said: When my father bowed, he would place his hand on His knees"
"2550","(2550) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, who said: I saw Abraham placing his hand on His knees"
"2551","(2551) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Nafi’, who said: I saw Sa`id bin Jubayr, when he bowed, and put his hands on me. His knees"
"2552","(2552) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, who said: Omar said: The knees have been made for you. So they held the knees. (Nasa’i 623)"
"2553","(2553) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Fitr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, he said: If you kneel, If you wish, you can say thus, and if you wish, you can place your hands on your knees, and if you wish, you can say thus, meaning: you applied it."
"2554","(2554) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The lions entered and attacked Abdullah, and Abdullah said: God: Have these people prayed yet? They said: No. He said: So stand up and pray. He did not order the call to prayer or the iqamah. He went ahead and led us in prayer, so we went to delay, so he took With our hands, so we stayed with him, and when we bowed down, the black man placed his hands on his knees, and Abdullah looked and saw him. So he struck his hand and looked at the black one, and saw Abdullah’s hands between his knees, and he had crossed his fingers. When he finished the prayer He said: If you are three, let one of you lead in prayer, and when you kneel, spread your arms and thighs, as if Look at the different fingers of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was bowing, then he said: There will be princes who will die. Prayer is at the east of the death, and it is the prayer of one who is worse than a donkey, and the prayer of one who does not have the means to have a living, so who among you realizes that? So let him perform the prayer at its appointed time, and let your prayer with them be a glorification of His glory. So I said to Abraham: It was Alqamiyah and the lions. Do they do that? He said: Yes, I said to Abraham: Do you do that? He said: Yes, I said: Do people put their hands on their knees? Ibrahim said: I heard Abu Muammar saying: I saw Omar putting his hands on his knees."
"2555","(2555) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: He taught us The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited the prayer, so he said “Allahu Akbar” and raised his hands, then he bowed and placed his hands between his knees. \n(Nasa’i 620 and Ibn Khuzaymah 595)"
"2556","(2556) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I said to Ibrahim: Did Abdullah use one hand to apply On the other, so he places them between his legs and spreads his arms and thighs when he bows? He said: Yes, I said: Should I not do that? He said: Omar used to put his palms on his knees."
"2557","(2557) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Othman bin Abi Hind narrated to us, saying: I saw Abu Ubaidah, when he bowed, he straightened."
"2558","(2558) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did it, meaning: he applied his hands while bowing. Ibn Aoun said: I mentioned it to Ibn Sirin, and he said: Perhaps he did it bitterly."
"2559","(2559) Hushaym told us, Hisham told us, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both; When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, would raise his head from bowing, he would say: Oh God, our Lord, to You is praise that fills the heavens and fills The earth and fill it with whatever you wish after that, the people of praise and glory. No one can hinder what You have given, and no one can give what You have withheld, and there is no benefit. This is the most serious of you. (Muslim 347. An-Nasa’i 654)"
"2560","(2560) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ubaid bin Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa; When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, raised his head from bowing, he would say: Oh God, our Lord, to You is praise that fills the heavens, and fills Earth, and fill it with whatever you wish after that. (Muslim 2020, Abu Dawud 842)"
"2561","(2561) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Zaid bin Abi Ziyad narrated to us, saying: Abu Juhayfa narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah; He used to say, when the imam raised his head from bowing, “O God, our Lord, praise be to You, fill the heavens, fill the earth, and fill what Whatever you want next."
"2562","(2562) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, he said: When Ali raised his head from bowing, he said: God hears those who praise Him. Oh God, our Lord, praise be to You. With Your power and strength I rise and sit."
"2563","(2563) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah bin Abdullah, He said: Qaz’a told us; When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, raised his head from bowing, he would say: Oh God, our Lord, to You is praise that fills the heavens and fills the earth. And fill it with whatever you wish after that. There is no one who can prevent what you have given, and there is no giver of what you withhold, and the hard worker will not benefit from the hard work from you. (Abu Dawud 843. An-Nasa’i 655)"
"2564","(2564) Yahya bin Abi Bukair told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Omar, on the authority of Abu Juhaifa; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up for prayer, and when he raised his head from bowing, he said: God hears those who praise Him, O God. Our Lord, to You is praise that fills the heavens and fills the earth, and fills whatever You wish after that. There is no hindrance to what You have given, and no giver of what You have withheld. Seriousness is of no use to you if he raises his voice with it. (Ibn Majah 879 and Abu Ali 882)"
"2565","(2565) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; When he raised his head, he would say: O God, our Lord, praise be to You."
"2566","(2566) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Burd; That Makhoul used to say when he raised his head from bowing: O God, our Lord, praise be to You. Fill the heavens and fill the earth, and fill whatever You wish. Nothing more, worthy of praise and praise, and the best thing a servant says, and we are all your servant, no one withholds what you have given, no one gives what You are forbidden, and seriousness will not benefit you."
"2567","(2567) Suwayd bin Amr Al-Kalbi told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Abi Salama told us, he said: Al-Majshun informed us My uncle, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Ali, who said: Whenever the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, raised He raised his head from bowing, and said: God hears those who praise Him. O God, our Lord, and to You is praise. Fill the heavens and fill the earth, and fill whatever You wish. Something more"
"2568","(2568) Ibn Numayr and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Mustarid bin Al-Ahnaf, On the authority of Sala bin Zufar, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: I prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his bowing was like He stood up, then said: God hears those who praise Him, then he stood for a long time. (Tirmidhi 262 and Abu Dawud 867)"
"2569","(2569) Ali told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: Whenever Omar raised his head from bowing, He said: God hears those who praise Him, before He raises His back."
"2570","(2570) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Al-Araj, he said: I heard Abu Hurairah raising his voice with: Oh God, our Lord, and you Praise"
"2571","(2571) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Salah, on the authority of Hudhayfa; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say in his bowing: Glory be to my Lord the Great, and in his prostration: Glory be to my Lord. Is it the highest? I said to Hafs: By praise? He said: Yes, God willing, three times. (Ibn Khuzaymah 668. Dar Qatni 341)"
"2572","(2572) Ibn Numayr and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Mustarid bin Al-Ahnaf, On the authority of Salah bin Zufar, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: I prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when he bowed, he began to say: Glory be to my Lord. The Great, then he prostrated and said: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High."
"2573","(2573) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Suhaim, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Ma’abad, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: As for bowing, glorify the Lord in it, and as for prostration, be diligent in supplications. It is certain that you will be answered. (Muslim 208 and Abu Dawud 872)"
"2574","(2574) Ibn Mushir and Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, on the authority of al-Nu’man ibn Sa’d, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I was forbidden to recite the Qur’an while bowing and prostrating, so when you kneel, glorify God, and when If you prostrated, then strive hard in the question, for it is certain that your supplication will be answered. (Abu Yali 297)"
"2575","(2575) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, who said: Three times of tasbihath when bowing. And prostration."
"2576","(2576) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, who said: I was informed that Omar used to say In bowing and prostrating, five tasbihs are recited: Glory be to God and praise be to Him."
"2577","(2577) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, he said: He said: Ali: When he bows Let one of you say: O God, to You I bowed, and to You I humbled myself, and in You I believed, and in You I put my trust, Glory be to my Lord the Great, three: And when he prostrates, he says: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High, three times, and if he is hurried by something, he says: Glory be to my Lord, the Great, and leaves that. Its parts (Muslim 201)"
"2578","(2578) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Farwa, on the authority of Ismail bin Ubaid Allah; He asked Abu Hurairah, and he said: I am a one-eyed man, so what do we say about glorification during prostration? He said: Three tasbihat."
"2579","(2579) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I prayed behind Omar bin Abdul Aziz, so I performed the bowing for him. Four or five tasbihahs, and in prostration five or six tasbihahs."
"2580","(2580) Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: Al-Hattaba came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said hello, and they said: O Messenger of God, we are always travelling, so what should we do with prayer? He said: Glorify God three times, bowing, and three times, prostrating. (Abdul Razzaq 2894)"
"2581","(2581) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to say: Whoever does not say “Tasbih” in his bowing and prostration, his prayer is only a staccato."
"2582","(2582) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to say: An average of bowing and prostration that a man says in his bowing and prostration: Glory be to God and praise be to Him, Three."
"2583","(2583) Hushaym told us, saying: Mansour told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to say: A complete prostration is equivalent to seven tasbihs, and what is sufficient is three."
"2584","(2584) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b; He heard him say: The minimum level of prostration when you place your head on the ground is to say: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High, three times."
"2585","(2585) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ajlah, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, he said: Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’ asked Abraham, and he said: How much praise does a man make when he lowers his head in prostration? So Abraham said: Three tasbihs."
"2586","(2586) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, who said: I asked Maimun about the extent of bowing and prostration? He said: I do not think it should be less than three times. Jafar said: So I asked Al-Zuhri, and he said: When the bones fall and become stable, I said to him: Auspicious man says: Three times of tasbihah. He said: I am telling you something like that."
"2587","(2587) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ziyad al-Musaffar, on the authority of al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: Three tasbihs. In bowing and prostration in the middle."
"2588","(2588) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, who said: Ali used to say when bowing: Glory be to Him. My Lord, the Great, three times, and in his prostration: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High, three times."
"2589","(2589) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shakhir, on the authority of Aisha; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say in his bowing and prostration: Glory be to the Holy One, Lord of the angels and the spirit. (Muslim 224, Abu Dawud 868)"
"2590","(2590) Waki’ and Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Ishaq ibn Zayd, on the authority of Awn ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: When one of you kneels, let him say: Glory be to my Lord. The Great, three times, and when he prostrates, let him say: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High, three times, for when he does that, his bowing has been completed. And his prostration, and that is the lowest. (Tirmidhi 261, Abu Dawud 882)"
"2591","(2591) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar; Ibn Masoud said while bowing: My Lord, forgive me."
"2592","(2592) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Ja’ad, a man from the people of Medina, on the authority of his son Sa’d; She used to bow too much, stooping awkwardly, and Saad said to her: It is enough for you if you place your hand on it. Your knees"
"2593","(2593) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, who said: If a man enables his hand to His knees, and the earth from his forehead, it is sufficient for him."
"2594","(2594) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of someone who heard Muhammad ibn Ali say: It is sufficient for him to bow when he places his hand on it. His knees, and it is part of prostration when he places his forehead on the ground."
"2595","(2595) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Malik, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: If a man gives birth I covered it with the earth in parts."
"2596","(2596) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: It is sufficient to perform bowing if possible. His hands are from his knees, and from prostration, if possible, his forehead is from the ground."
"2597","(2597) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Ali bin Hakim, who said: Tawoos and Ikrimah said, And I think a third gift is: If he can collect his portion of land, then he has paid what he owes."
"2598","(2598) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, who said: If he places his jilbab on the ground, then Its parts"
"2599","(2599) Hafs told us, on the authority of Maqil bin Ubaid Allah, who said: I asked Ata’ about the minimum permissible bowing and prostration? He said: When he puts his forehead on the ground, and puts his hands on his knees."
"2600","(2600) It was narrated, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If he places his hand on His knees and his parts."
"2601","(2601) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hussein Al-Mukhtab, on the authority of Badil, on the authority of Abu Al-Jawzai, on the authority of Aisha, She said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, bowed, he would not turn his head towards himself or direct it. He was in between."
"2602","(2602) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman, on the authority of a man from Thaqif, who said: I asked Abu Hurairah, and he said: : Beware of tenderness in bowing and humping."
"2603","(2603) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: When you kneel, keep your face upright. For the kiss, put your hands on your knees, and do not slaughter like a donkey."
"2604","(2604) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He disliked a man raising his head when he was bowing, or pointing at it."
"2605","2605) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid; He disliked leaning towards one another while bowing."
"2606","(2606) Muadh bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Habib bin Al-Shahid, who said: I heard Muhammad bin Sirin say: Bowing like this, Muadh described that he straightened his back, neither straightening his head nor raising it. He said: I heard Al-Hasan say something like that. However, Al-Hasan spoke about it verbally."
"2607","(2607) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Abu Farwa, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was Peace and blessings of God be upon him, when he bows, if you pour water on his shoulders, he will stand still. (Tabarani 12755; Abd al-Razzaq 2872)"
"2608","(2608) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: If the imam says: God hears those who praise Him, then say: Oh God, our Lord, praise be to You."
"2609","(2609) Hushaym told us, he said: Omar bin Abi Salamah told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he narrated it, he said: And if the imam says: God hears those who praise Him, then say: O God, our Lord, to You be praise. (Bukhari 722. Muslim 309)"
"2610","(2610) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Yunus bin Jubayr, on the authority of Hattan bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If the imam says: God hears those who praise Him, then say: Oh God, our Lord, praise be to You. God hears you. (Muslim 403. Ahmad 4/409)"
"2611","(2611) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The imam has only been appointed to be followed, so when he bows, bow down, and when he says: God hears To those who praise Him, say: Oh God, our Lord, praise be to You. (Muslim 306. Abu Dawud 604)"
"2612","(2612) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: If the imam says: God hears To the one who praised Him, those behind him said: O God, our Lord, praise be to You."
"2613","(2613) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Aamir, who said: The people should not say behind the imam: “God hears those who praise Him.” But to say: O God, our Lord, praise be to You."
"2614","(2614) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Zuhair bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, On the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, that he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: If he said Your imam: God hears those who praise Him, so say: O God, our Lord, praise be to You. (Ahmed 3/3)"
"2615","(2615) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Muhammad used to say, when he said: God hears those who praise Him, he said: Who Behind him: God hears those who praise Him. O God, our Lord, praise be to You."
"2616","(2616) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of a man from the people of Medina, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace; He heard the beating of his shoes while he was prostrating, so when he finished his prayer, he said: Who is this whose shoes I heard beating? He said: I am, O Messenger of God. He said: What did you do? He said: I found you prostrating, so I prostrated. So he said: So do it, and do not neglect it. Whoever finds me bowing, or prostrating, or standing. Let him be with me as I am.\n(Abdul Razzaq 3373, Bayhaqi 89)"
"2617","(2617) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of a man from the Ansar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace; In the same way"
"2618","(2618) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar and Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: He found them and they had raised their heads from bowing, so he said “Allahu Akbar” and prostrated, but he did not care about them."
"2619","(2619) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan (h), and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who approaches the imam while he is prostrating. They said: He follows him and prostrates with him, and does not differ from him, nor does he violate him. In prostration unless he overtakes the bowing."
"2620","(2620) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: In what condition did you catch up with the Imam, but no You disagree with him."
"2621","(2621) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Salam bin Abi Dhayal, on the authority of his followers, who said: If you catch them prostrating, then prostrate. with them, and do not observe that rak’ah."
"2622","(2622) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: If you find them prostrating, then prostrate with them, and do not neglect them. With it, and Abu Al-Aaliyah said: Prostrate with them and observe it."
"2623","(2623) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: In what condition did you find the Imam? So do as he does."
"2624","(2624) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: In any case, you find the Imam, so do so. As he does"
"2625","(2625) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: It was desirable for the people not to overtake you in any state. In prayer, unless he enters it with them."
"2626","(2626) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a man who approaches the people while they are prostrating, he said: He will prostrate with them."
"2627","(2627) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin, who said: A man should not stand upright. And the people have lowered their heads."
"2628","(2628) Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; It was disliked for a man, if he came while the imam was prostrating, to stand still so that he could follow him."
"2629","(2629) Hammad bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi al-Mawali, on the authority of Omar bin Abi Muslim, who said: It was Urwa Ibn Al-Zubayr says: If one of you comes while the imam is prostrating, let him prostrate with the people, and should not be taken into account."
"2630","(2630) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubaira, on the authority of Ali, he said: No. Prostration is counted if he does not perform bowing."
"2631","(2631) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, he said: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas and Hubayra, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: If you do not know how to bow, then do not count the prostration."
"2632","(2632) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of his father, who said: Abdullah ibn Zayd al-Khattimi was When he raises his head from the rak’ah and shouts “Allahu Akbar”, it is as if he is in a sway until he prostrates."
"2633","(2633) Ali told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: When Omar raised his head from bowing, he said: God hears those who praise Him, before He raises His back, and when He says Allahu Akbar, He says Allahuu Akbar while he is low."
"2634","(2634) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Say “Allahu Akbar” while you are lost, and you kneel down"
"2635","(2635) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, saying: A partner informed us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Omar; He used to chant takbeer."
"2636","(2636) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Whenever Omar said: God hears those who praise Him, he would recoil. magnifying"
"2637","(2637) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahhab, who said: I went out with Abdullah from his house to The mosque. When we reached the middle of the mosque, the imam kneeled, and Abdullah said “Allahu Akbar,” then he bowed and I kneeled with him, then we walked, bowing. Until we reached the ranks, until the people raised their heads. He said: When the imam finished the prayer, I got up and saw that I did not catch you, so he took Abdullah by the hand and made me sit, and said: You have come. I realized"
"2638","(2638) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; That Abu Ubaidah came while the people were bowing, so he kneeled below the row, then he walked until he entered the row, then he narrated, on the authority of his father, Like that"
"2639","(2639) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Imamah; That Zayd ibn Thabit bowed before he reached the row, then he walked, bowing."
"2640","(2640) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mawīb, on the authority of Kathir ibn Aflah, on the authority of Zaid Bin Thabit; He entered while the people were bowing, so he kneeled below the row, then entered the row."
"2641","(2641) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Yazid, who said: I saw Ibn Jubayr, so he did it."
"2642","(2642) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, who said: My father used to enter while the imam was bowing, so he would kneel without the row. Then he enters the class."
"2643","(2643) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Waqa’i, who said: Sa’id bin Jubayr and I entered while they were bowing, so I and he among the others kneeled. The door, then we came until we entered the classroom."
"2644","(2444) Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Ayyub, who said: Yazid bin Abi narrated to me. lover; He saw Abu Salamah entering the mosque and the people were bowing, so he bowed, then he returned to bow."
"2645","(2645) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning one who enters the mosque while the imam is bowing, he said: If he passes the women, he says “Allahu Akbar” and bows, then proceeds until he enters the row. He made prostration catch him. Before that, he prostrated wherever he reached it."
"2646","(2446) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, who said: Amr bin Tamim and I entered the mosque, and the imam knelt down. So he and I knelt down, and we walked on our knees until we entered the row. When we finished the prayer, Amr said to me: What you just did from among those who Did you hear it? I said: From Mujahid. He said: I saw Ibn al-Zubayr, so he did it."
"2647","(2647) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Al-Qasim (h) and Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Concerning the man entering the mosque while the people had bowed down. He said: If he thought that he would overtake the people before they rose. Their heads, let him kneel, and let him walk until he enters the row."
"2648","(2648) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Do not say takbeer until You take your place in the class."
"2649","(2649) Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of Abu al-Mu’ali, who said: Al-Hasan was asked about a man who kneels before he reaches the line? He said: He does not kneel."
"2650","(2650) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I said to Abraham: If I enter the mosque and the imam is bowing, I bow before Did you go to class? He said: You don't do that."
"2651","(2651) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: If you enter And the imam is bowing, so do not kneel until you take your place in the row. Abu Bakr said: If it is him and another, he kneels without the row, and if he is alone, he does not kneel."
"2652","(2652) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, he said: When Mujahid bowed, he would place his hands on his knees. He said: A giving, a peacock, and a beneficial one they release."
"2653","(2653) Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Hafs, on the authority of Laith, who said: A man prayed next to Ata’, and when he bowed, he bent his knees. He said, so he struck his hand and said: Spread them out."
"2654","(2654) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Salim Al-Barrad, who said: We came to Abu Masoud in his house. So we said to him: We knew the prayer of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he prayed, and when he prostrated, he cupped his elbows. (Abu Dawud 859. An-Nasa’i 624)"
"2655","(2655) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Burqan, on the authority of Yazid ibn al-Asam, on the authority of Maimunah, she said: The Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, when he prostrates, those behind him will see the whites of his armpits. (Muslim 357. Abu Dawud 894)"
"2656","(2656) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abbad bin Rashid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Ahmar, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated to me. And peace be upon him. He said: Indeed, we would seek refuge with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from what is far from my side when he prostrates.\n(Abu Dawud 8968, Ibn Majah 886)"
"2657","(2657) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Qays, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Aqram Al-Khuza’i, on the authority of his father He said: I was with my father in Al-Qaa near Nimra, when a group of people passed by us and they stopped in the direction of the road. He said: Son, be there. With you until these people came, so he went out and I went out with him, that is, he approached and approached, and behold, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He prayed, and I prayed with him, and I was looking at his armpits. (Ibn Majah 881. Ahmad 4/35)"
"2658","(2658) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Shu`ba, the client of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It was The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sees the whites of his armpits when he prostrates. (Abu Dawud 895. Ahmad 1/267)"
"2659","(2659) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Humayd, who said: When Anas prostrated, he would be upright."
"2660","(2660) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to see those behind him the whites of his armpits when he prostrated."
"2661","(2661) Hashim bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, who said: Asim bin Shammikh Al-Ghaylani, one of the sons of Tamim, he said: I entered upon Abu Saeed and saw him prostrating, with his elbows extended by his side, until I could see him. The whites of her armpits."
"2662","(2662) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A man avoids you."
"2663","(2663) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: If a man prostrates, let him be silent."
"2664","(2664) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When a man prostrates, let him spread his thighs apart."
"2665","(2665) Aswad bin Amir narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: He described Al-Bara’ to us, so he relied on his sufficiency. He raised his crotch and said: This is how the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to prostrate. (Abu Dawud 892. Ahmad 4/303)"
"2666","(2646) Hafs bin Ghayath, Abu Muawiyah, and Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When one of you prostrates, let him stand upright, and not spread his arms wide apart. The dog\n(Tirmidhi 275. Ahmad 3/305)"
"2667","(2667) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Jafar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Tamim bin Mahmoud, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Shibl said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade sleeping with wild animals. (Abu Dawud 858, Darmi 1323)"
"2668","(2668) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: If one of you prostrates Let him be straight, and not spread his arms like a dog."
"2669","(2669) Yazeed bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn al-Mukhtab, on the authority of Badil, on the authority of Abu al-Jawzai, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade one of us spreading his arms like a snake."
"2670","(2670) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Be moderate. In your prostration, let none of you spread out his arms as a dog does. (Bukhari 822 and Abu Dawud 893)"
"2671","(2671) Muawiyah bin Amr narrated to us, saying: Zayed narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Salih bin Khabab, on the authority of Husain bin Uqba, on the authority of Omar (h) and on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: When he prostrates Let one of you stand straight and not spread his arms like a dog."
"2672","(2672) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha’, on the authority of al-Hakam ibn al-Araj, who said: Tell me who saw Abu Dharr blackened. From between his wrists to his elbows."
"2673","(2673) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Aamir ibn Abdah, he said: Abdullah said: The bones of the son of Adam were prepared for his prostration. Prostrate, even with your elbows."
"2674","(2674) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I said to Muhammad: A man prostrates, leaning on his elbows. His knees? He said: I do not know of any harm in it."
"2675","(2675) Asim told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar used to clasp his hands to his sides when He prostrated."
"2676","(2676) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ash’ath ibn Abi al-Sha’tha’i, on the authority of Qays ibn Sakan, who said: All of this has happened. They used to do it, they would join each other and separate themselves, some of them would join in and some of them would withdraw from each other."
"2677","(2677) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Sumayyah, on the authority of Al-Nu’man ibn Abi Ayyash, who said: They complained to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He granted support and reliance in prayer, and permitted them to allow a man to rest his elbows on his knees, or His thighs\n(Abdul Razzaq 2928)"
"2678","(2678) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Habib, who said: A man asked Ibn Umar: I place my elbows on my thighs if Did you prostrate? He said: Prostrate as it is easy for you."
"2679","(2679) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, who said: Abdullah said: If If you prostrate, then prostrate even with your elbows, meaning he should use his elbows for help."
"2680","(2680) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: He was asked: Where was the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him? And he laid his face down? He said: He used to place it between his palms, or he said: His hands, meaning in prostration."
"2681","(2681) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wa’il ibn Hajar, he said: I said: Let us look at it. The prayer of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So he prostrated, and I saw his head from his hand, the same size as he had opened."
"2682","(2682) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wa’il ibn Hajar, he said: I saw When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrated, his hands were close to his ears. (Ahmad 4/316. Ibn Hibban 1860)"
"2683","(2683) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Salem Al-Barrad, who said: We came to Abu Masoud Al-Ansari about His house, so we said: We taught the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he prayed. Then when he prostrated, he placed his palm close to the His head"
"2684","(2684) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He was asked about a man who prostrates, how should he place his hands? He said: He places them wherever he can, or however they come."
"2685","(2685) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, he said: I said to Ibn Umar: I will be in the class and in it. Tightness, how do I put my hands? He said: Put them where you can."
"2686","(2686) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: They used to like, when a man prostrated, to say with his hand. Thus, Azhar joined his fingers."
"2687","(2687) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When you prostrate, do not close your palms together. And spread out your fingers."
"2688","(2688) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, who said: I prayed next to Hafs ibn Asim, when I prostrated, I spread my fingers together and tilted my palm away from the direction of the direction. When I made the salutation, he said: O son of my brother, when you prostrate, press your hands together. Your fingers, and the face of your hand before the qiblah, for the hands prostrate with the face."
"2689","(2689) Waki’ told us, Sufyan said: He spreads his fingers apart when bowing, and closes them when prostrating."
"2690","(2690) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: Prostration upon Aliyah. The palm\n(Ibn Khuzaymah 639. Ibn Hibban 1915)"
"2691","(2691) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Al-Bara’ bin Azib saying: Prostration upon Aliyah. The two palms"
"2692","(2692) Yahya bin Saeed and Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Amer bin Saad said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered that the palms be placed and the feet be placed in prostration.\n(Tirmidhi 272 and Abu Dawud 888)"
"2693","(2693) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: The greatest prostration is on the two palms. And the knees and the tops of the feet."
"2694","(2694) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Talq ibn Habib; In his saying: {And the faces are meant for the Ever-Living, the Ever-Subsisting} He said: prostrating on the forehead, the palms, and the knees. And the feet."
"2695","(2695) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Omar, who said: The son of Adam was directed to prostrate on seven limbs; The forehead, the palms, the knees, and the feet."
"2696","(2696) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Bishr told us, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Prostrating on seven limbs; The forehead, the palms, the knees, and the feet."
"2697","(2697) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: I was commanded to prostrate on seven pillars, without a shackle of hair or clothing. (Bukhari 812, Muslim 231)"
"2698","(2698) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: They used to like to prostrate on seven great people; On the hands, knees, feet, and forehead."
"2699","(2699) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: He prostrates on seven greater ones; His hands, his feet, his forehead, and his knees."
"2700","(2700) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad; He hated to prostrate with his toes facing like this. He described that he bent it to the inside of his foot, and said: Spread it out."
"2701","(2701) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Al-Anbas, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, who said: When you prostrate, put the accusative Your feet"
"2702","(2702) Hushaym and Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abdul-Jabbar bin Wa’il, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrates on his forehead and nose."
"2703","(2703) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he used to say: When he prostrates Let one of you stick his nose to the sink, for God has desired that from you."
"2704","(2704) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Prostration is on the forehead and nose."
"2705","(2705) Mutalib bin Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Isa, who said: Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla and I passed by. He prostrated, and said: O son of Jesus, place your nose before God."
"2706","(2706) Ibn Fadil told us, on the authority of Waqa’i, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: I heard him say: A man’s prayer is not complete. Until it touches his nose as it touches his forehead."
"2707","(2707) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, he said: Were you informed that a peacock was asked about prostrating on the nose? He said: Isn’t he the most honorable face?"
"2708","(2708) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, who said: When Ibn Sirin prostrated on a place where his nose would not touch the ground, He moved to another place."
"2709","(2709) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Thabit bin Qais, who said: I saw Nafi bin Jubayr touching his nose to the ground."
"2710","(2710) Ibn Fadil told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a man. He was prostrating, not placing his nose on the ground, and he said: Whoever prays a prayer that does not strike the nose what strikes the forehead, his prayer will not be accepted. (Daraqutni 348, Bayhaqi 3)"
"2711","(2711) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; When he prostrated, he would place his nose on his forehead."
"2712","(2712) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Ubaid Allah, he said: I said to Wahab bin Kaysan: Abu Naim, why do you not keep your forehead and nose off the ground? He said: That is because I heard Jabir bin Abdullah saying: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrating at the top of Her forehead is covered with hair clips. (Daraqutni 349. Tabarani 435)"
"2713","(2713) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If you wish, prostrate on your nose, and if you wish, do not do so."
"2714","(2714) Ma’n narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Bakr, who said: I saw Al-Qasim and Salim prostrating on their foreheads, and no Their noses touch the ground."
"2715","(2715) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; Concerning a man who did not prostrate on his nose, he said: That is sufficient."
"2716","(2716) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: It will not harm him."
"2717","(2717) Ibn Fadil narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and it is narrated that He said: When one of you prostrates, he should start with his knees before his hands, and do not bless the brook of a stallion. (Abu Dawud 834, Tahawi 255, Bayhaqi 100)"
"2718","(2718) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim; Omar used to place his knees before his hands."
"2719","(2718) Ali told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad; Omar was falling on his knees."
"2720","(2720) Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to lower his knees when he prostrated before his hands, and raise his hands when he prostrated before his knees."
"2721","(2721) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Khams, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim bin Yassar, on the authority of his father; When he prostrated, his knees would fall, then his hands, then his head."
"2722","(2722) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He was asked about a man who places his hands before his knees? He thought about it and said: Would anyone do it except a madman?!"
"2723","(2723) Abbad ibn al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Khalid, he said: I saw Abu Qalababi, when he prostrated, he would start and place his knees. And when he gets up, he leans on his hands, and I see Al-Hasan falling down, and he starts with his hands, and he leans on his hands when he gets up."
"2724","(2724) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Mahdi bin Maimun, who said: I saw Ibn Sirin bowing his knees before... His hands"
"2725","(2725) Mu`tamar told us, on the authority of Muammar, he said: His followers were asked about a man who, if he stands up from bowing, starts with his hand? He said: This is easier for him to do."
"2726","(2726) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: Whenever Abdullah’s companions went down to prostrate, Their knees before their hands."
"2727","(2727) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Harithah, on the authority of Umar, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was When he prostrates, peace be upon him, he places his hands facing the qiblah."
"2728","(2728) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to say: When he prostrates One of you should face the Qiblah with his hands, for they prostrate with their faces facing."
"2729","(2729) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad; When they prostrated, they both liked to face each other towards the direction of the qiblah."
"2730","(2730) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Uthman Al-Thaqafi; Aisha saw a man leaning with his palm towards the direction of the direction of prayer, so she said: Turn them both towards the direction of the direction of direction."
"2731","(2731) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Abdul Rahman ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Hafs ibn Asim, who said: Who The Sunnah in prayer is to spread out your palms, join your fingers, and turn them with your face towards the Qiblah."
"2732","(2732) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Bakr, who said: I saw Salim and Al-Qasim, when they prostrated, facing each other. With their palms facing the qiblah."
"2733","(2733) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Mis`ar, on the authority of Uthman, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar: He hated to be fair with his sufficiency. About the Qibla"
"2734","(2734) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Mis’ar told us, on the authority of Uthman, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, Such as a comprehensive hadith."
"2735","(2735) Hushaym told us, he said: Mujalid told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Sa’id bin Dhu La’awiya, he said: Omar said: If If one of you is able to prostrate on the day of Friday, let him prostrate on the back of his brother."
"2736","(2736) Hushaym told us, saying: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham; He used to say that."
"2737","(2737) Hushaym told us, saying: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Because he liked to stand until they raised their heads, then he would prostrate."
"2738","(2738) Abdul Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Tawus, who said: If he is not able On the day of Friday prayer, he should prostrate on the ground and turn his head, so he should prostrate on his brother’s back."
"2739","(2739) A partner told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abdul Karim, who said: Mujahid said: Should I prostrate on the back of a man? He said: Yes."
"2740","(2740) Ishaq bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Anbasa, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, He said: When the one between his hands raises his head, he prostrates."
"2741","(2741) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, on the authority of Omar, he said: If A man can prostrate on Friday, so let him prostrate on his brother’s back."
"2742","(2742) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Omar said, then he mentioned something like the hadith of my father. Mu'awiyah, on the authority of Al-A'mash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab."
"2743","(2743) Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abd The Most Gracious, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to us and he led us in prayer in the mosque of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, and I saw him laying His hands are in his garment when he prostrates. (Ibn Majah 1031. Ahmad 4/335)"
"2744","(2744) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, or Bura, who said: Ibn Umar used to wrap himself in a quilt, then He prostrates in it."
"2745","(2745) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Al-Duha, who said: I saw Shurayh prostrating in his cloak."
"2746","(2746) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father; He used to prostrate in a cloak, and would not take his hands out of it."
"2747","(2747) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, who said: I saw the lion praying in his robe, prostrating In it, I saw Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Yazid, praying in a Syrian garment, prostrating in it."
"2748","(2748) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to prostrate in the folds of his tongue."
"2749","(2749) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: I saw Yahya bin Wattab praying in a watering hole between Two pillars. He leads the people in prayer, with his hands in their hollows."
"2750","(2750) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Humaid, who said: I saw Al-Hassan wearing a scarf in the winter, praying. In it, and he does not take his hand out of it."
"2751","(2751) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Nafi’; I saw Saeed bin Jubayr praying in a robe, and he did not remove his hands from it."
"2752","(2752) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: Alqamiya and Masruq used to pray in their cloaks. And their provisions, and they do not cast out their hands."
"2753","(2753) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhall, who said: I saw Abraham not taking his hands out of the water."
"2754","(2754) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrate And their hands are in their clothes, and one of them prostrates on his turban."
"2755","(2755) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Khaled; When Abu Qulabab prostrated, he would take his hand out of his garment."
"2756","(2756) Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Asama bin Zaid, who said: I saw Salim, when he prostrated, he took his hands out of the With his robe, until he places them on the ground."
"2757","(2757) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad used to touch the palm of the earth when he prostrated."
"2758","(2758) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Asim, On the authority of Abu Hind al-Shami, he said: Omar said: When one of you prostrates, let him face the palm of the earth, perhaps God will turn away from him. Excessive, indeed, exaggerated on the Day of Resurrection."
"2759","(2759) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibn Abi al-Hudhayl; When he wanted to prostrate, he would remove his hand from the pad."
"2760","(2760) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad; That Ibn Omar used to take out his hands when he prostrated, and they would drip blood."
"2761","(2761) Malik bin Ismail told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Ishaq bin Suwayd told us, he said: I saw a father When Qadawi al-Adawi prostrates, he takes out his hands and touches them to the ground."
"2762","(2762) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid; He used to prostrate on the balls of his turban."
"2763","(2763) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab and Al-Hasan, that they were not He sees strength in prostrating on the turban’s sleeves."
"2764","(2764) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to prostrate on the balls of his turban."
"2765","(2765) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr; He used to prostrate while he was blind."
"2766","(2766) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Rashid, on the authority of Makhoul; He used to prostrate on the inside of his turban, so I said to him? He said: I fear for my eyesight from the cold pebbles."
"2767","(2767) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far bin Burqan, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: There is no harm in prostrating on the turban’s sleeves."
"2768","(2768) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Warqa’, who said: I saw Ibn Abi Awfa prostrating on a hill. His turban"
"2769","(2769) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, who said: I saw Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid prostrating to His turban is thick in colours, it has come between his forehead and the earth."
"2770","(2770) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sakan bin Abi Karimah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ubadah, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Rabi’, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit; When he stood up for prayer, he would remove the turban from his forehead."
"2771","(2771) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abd al-A’la al-Thaalabi, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Ali, he said: When one of you prays, let him uncover the turban from his forehead."
"2772","(2772) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar did not prostrate on a corner. The turban"
"2773","(2773) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: A grief struck me, so I tied a bandage on her, so she asked Ubaidah: Should I prostrate to her? He said: No. (Abdul Razzaq 1569)"
"2774","(2774) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Saleh, on the authority of Iyad bin Abdullah Al-Qurashi; He said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw a man prostrating on the balls of his turban, so he motioned with his hand to remove your turban. So he gestured to his forehead."
"2775","(2775) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He used to like the dark hair to remove the turban balls from his forehead."
"2776","(2776) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Zubayr ibn Adiy, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The one that sticks out my forehead is more beloved to me."
"2777","(2777) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad; He disliked prostrating on the turban’s sleeves."
"2778","(2778) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hafar bin Burqan, on the authority of Maimun, who said: If my forehead is exposed, it is more beloved to me."
"2779","(2779) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He disliked prostrating on the turban’s sleeves."
"2780","(2780) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father; In Al-Mu'tam, he said: He should cover his forehead with the ground."
"2781","(2781) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Ulatha, that Omar bin Abdul Aziz said to a man: Perhaps you are among those who prostrate on a corner. Turbans?!"
"2782","(2782) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Ja’adah bin Hubaira; He saw a man prostrating while wearing a robe and a turban. He had covered his face with them, so he took his robe and turban with them. So he threw him behind him."
"2783","(2783) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: One day Omar prayed with all the people together, On a very hot day, he threw the edge of his garment on the ground and began to prostrate on it, then he said: O people, when he finds If any of you is free, let him prostrate on the edge of his garment."
"2784","(2784) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, on the authority of Omar, he said: If If one of you is able to prostrate on the ground from the heat or the cold, let him prostrate on his garment."
"2785","(2785) Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, on the authority of Ghalib, on the authority of Bakr, on the authority of Anas, who said: We used to pray with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He saluted in the intense heat. If one of us was not able to raise his face from the ground, he spread his garment and prostrated over it.\n(Muslim 1911, Abu Dawud 660)"
"2786","(2786) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed in one garment, protecting himself from the heat and cold of the earth. (Ahmad 1/354; Abd al-Razzaq 1369)"
"2787","(2787) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Umar said: If one of you finds the heat of the land, let him put His garment is between him and the earth, then he will prostrate on it."
"2788","(2788) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham, that he said: When it is hot or cold Let him prostrate on his garment."
"2789","(2789) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim, who said: I saw a mujahid in the Sacred Mosque one day. Hot, he spread his garment and prostrated over it."
"2790","(2790) Zaid bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saeed, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, who said: I said to Ata bin Yasar: Should I prostrate on my dress? He said: My clothes are made of semen."
"2791","(2791) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He did not see any harm in a man prostrating over a garment."
"2792","(2792) Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I prostrate on my garment when the heat hurts me, As for the appearance of a man, no."
"2793","(2793) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: When a woman prostrates, let her be alert. And embrace her thighs."
"2794","(2794) Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abi Ayyub, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He was asked about a woman’s prayer? He said: You gather and celebrate."
"2795","(2795) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When a woman prostrates, she should hold her thighs together. And let her put her belly on them."
"2796","(2796) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; He disliked it for a man to place his stomach on his thighs when he prostrated, as a woman does."
"2797","(2797) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The woman squeezes during prostration."
"2798","(2798) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When a woman prostrates, she should touch her stomach. With her thighs, and do not raise her crotch, and do not touch her as a man does."
"2799","(2799) Ismail Ibn Ali told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Zur’a Ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Khalid Ibn Al-Lajlaj, He said: Women were commanded to cross-legged themselves when they sat during prayer, and not to sit on their hips as men do, so as to be pious. This is for the woman, for fear that something might be part of her."
"2800","(2800) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Nafi’; Safiyya used to pray while sitting cross-legged."
"2801","(2801) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Makhoul; Umm al-Darda’ used to sit during prayer like a man would sit."
"2802","(2802) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Squatting."
"2803","(2803) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Salam, on the authority of his leaders, who said: You sit as you see that it is easier."
"2804","(2804) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The woman sits during prayer as he sits. The man"
"2805","(2805) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar’s wives used to sit next to each other during prayer."
"2806","(2806) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Hammad about a woman sitting during prayer? He said: You may sit however you wish."
"2807","(2807) Muhammad Ibn Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: I said to Ata’: Does a woman sit in a folded place on two sides? The left one? He said: Yes, I said: Is he more beloved to you than the right hand? He said: Yes, she gathers while sitting as long as she is able. I said: She sits like a man in a flexed position, or she puts her left leg out from under her. What is it? He said: It does not matter if she sits when she gathers."
"2808","(2808) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A woman sits on one side during prayer."
"2809","(2809) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, and Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: A woman sits in prayer as facilitate"
"2810","(2810) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, who said: I saw the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He gave the salutation, not raising his hands between the two prostrations. (Bukhari 738 and Abu Dawud 721)"
"2811","(2811) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salma, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Anas; He used to raise his hands between the two prostrations."
"2812","(2812) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to raise his hand when he raised his head from the first prostration."
"2813","(2813) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, he said: I saw Nafi’ and Tawoos raising their hands between the two prostrations."
"2814","(2814) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin; They used to raise their hands between the two prostrations."
"2815","(2815) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, he said: I saw him do it."
"2816","(2816) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu, so he visited him, he said: Ibn Abbas said: The sick person prostrates on The elbow and the good clothes."
"2817","(2817) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Umm Al-Hasan narrated to me; She saw Umm Salamah’s eyes darken, so I made a human pillow for her, and she began to prostrate on it."
"2818","(2818) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Umm Salamah, the same."
"2819","(2819) Ali bin Musahir narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Umm Salamah, the same, except that he said: Her eyes complained."
"2820","(2820) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Anas; He prostrated on his elbow."
"2821","(2821) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Khalda, who said: Abu Al-Aaliyah was ill, and the elbow was She bends over to him and he prostrates to her."
"2822","(2822) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He saw no harm in a man prostrating on the elbow and the pillow in the ship."
"2823","(2823) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’; Ibn Omar Safwan came back and found him prostrating on a pillow, so he stopped him and said: Nod."
"2824","(2824) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Prostrating on a pillow is an innovation."
"2825","(2825) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Dawud ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Harb ibn Abi Al-Aswad, he said: Abu complained The black man, he would not prostrate except to what We had raised him for, and he would prostrate on it at an elbow, so we asked about that, and he was sent to Ibn Omar, and he said: If he is able, he should prostrate on the ground, otherwise he should gesture."
"2826","(2826) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas; He used to pray on his bed."
"2827","(2827) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos; He was praying on the bed on which he fell ill."
"2828","(2828) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaidullah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I saw the lions gesticulating. His illness"
"2829","(2829) Hatem bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala; He saw Saeed bin Al-Musayyab that if he was sick and could not sit, he would nod and did not raise anything to his head."
"2830","(2830) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that they said: He prays. The sick person is in the condition he is in."
"2831","(2831) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Tamimah, his servant and his servant, who said: Shurayh entered upon Abu Misra. He came back and said to him: How do you pray? He said: sitting, he said: Then Shurayh said to him: You are more knowledgeable than us."
"2832","(2832) Abd al-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, that he used to say: If the sick person is unable Prostrating, gesturing."
"2833","(2833) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, who said: I asked Amir about the sick person’s prayer? He said: If he is not able to place his forehead on the ground, then he should gesture and make the prostration lower than the bowing."
"2834","(2834) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabalah ibn Suhaim, who said: I asked Ibn Umar about the sick person’s prayer on the oud? He said: I do not command you to take idols other than God. If you are able, you should pray standing, otherwise, then sitting, otherwise, then lying down."
"2835","(2835) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, who said: We entered upon Abraham while he was sick, and he He prays on his right side, gesticulating."
"2836","(2836) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us on the authority of Abu Khalda, who said: I saw Abu al-Aaliyah while he was sick and was vomiting."
"2837","(2837) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: He prays sitting, if he does not He can nod, but does not touch a stick."
"2838","(2838) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Rabah bin Abi Marouf, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a sick person, if he is unable to pray, he said: He gestures."
"2839","(2839) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Abu Awani told us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith, he said: He prays If the sick person is unable to sit down, he should place his feet on the side facing him, and face him. Qiblah, nodding his head."
"2840","(2840) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar bin Falfil, he said: I asked Anas about the sick person’s prayer. How does he pray? He said: He prays sitting, and prostrates on the ground."
"2841","(2841) Hammad bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid, the client of Urwa, on the authority of Urwa, who said: The sick person is a mummy, and he does not He raises something to his face."
"2842","(2842) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Khushina, Ibn Omar’s chamberlain, who said: I entered with Al-Hakam bin Al-Araj on Bakr Al-Muzani. While he was sick, he said: Did you pray the afternoon prayer? They said: Yes, so he stood up and prayed a prayer, which he made short of it due to his illness."
"2843","(2843) Affan narrated to us, he said: Saeed bin Zaid narrated to us, he said: Abu Abdullah Al-Shaqri narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Raja’. Ibn Rabi’a, on the authority of his father, he said: We were with Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri during his illness in which he died. He said: Then he fainted, and when he woke up, he said: We said to him: Prayer, O Abu Sa’id. He said: It is enough.\n Abu Bakr said: He means Kafan, meaning he nodded."
"2844","(2844) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Asim told us, he said: Abu Wael came in when I was sick, So I said to him: Should I pray, Abu Wael, when I am numb? He said: Yes."
"2845","(2845) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Muzani, who said: Omar hated him. For a man to prostrate on a stick."
"2846","(2846) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, who said: Abdullah entered upon his brother’s household. He went back and found him praying on a stick, so he threw him out and said: This is something that Satan has done to him. Place your face on the ground. If you cannot, then nod."
"2847","(2847) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: He was asked about praying on the oud and he thought about it."
"2848","(2848) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, who said: Ibn Masoud entered upon his brother’s household while he was ill. He was prostrating on a siwak, so he threw it away and said: “Make a gesture.”"
"2849","(2849) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He disliked praying on the oud."
"2850","(2850) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, on the authority of Malik bin Umayr, he said: Someone who saw it told me Hudhayf fell ill, so he was praying, and a pillow had been made for him, and a board had been made for him to prostrate on."
"2851","(2851) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Razin, the client of the Abbas family, who said: Ali bin Abdullah bin Abbas sent me, Send me a tablet of marwa, I will prostrate on it."
"2852","(2852) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Abdullah Ali entered upon his brother and saw him praying. On a stick, so he pulled it out and threw it, saying: Nod as far as your head reaches."
"2853","(2853) Azhar Al-Samman told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad; Concerning a sick person, if he is not able to prostrate, he said: He gestures as far as his head reaches."
"2854","(2854) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had three silences: He remained silent when he opened the takbeer until he recited al-Hamd, and when he finished saying al-Hamd until he recited the surah, and when he finished saying Surah until he kneels. (Tirmidhi 251, Abu Dawud 776)"
"2855","(2855) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Amara ibn al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: It was When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said “Allahu Akbar,” he remained silent between saying “Allahu Akbar” and reciting it. (Bukhari 744, Abu Dawud 777)"
"2856","(2856) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Amr bin Muhajir, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: He had two stops: A pause when he says “Allahu Akbar”, and a pause when he finishes the Umm al-Kitab."
"2857","(2857) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah bin Jundub, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he would remain silent twice: when he entered into the prayer, and when he finished the recitation, and he denied that. Imran bin Husayn, so they wrote to Ubayy bin Ka’b, and he wrote to them saying the truth about Samara. (Abu Dawud 773. Ahmad 5/23)"
"2858","(2858) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; When he said Allahu Akbar, he would remain silent in peace, and when he said: “None of those with anger upon them, nor those who have gone astray,” he would remain silent in peace. And when he got up in the second rak’ah, he did not remain silent and said: {Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds}"
"2859","(2859) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Imam remained silent two times: He remained silent when he said the greatest before he said: He recites, and remains silent when he finishes the surah before he bows."
"2860","(2860) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari, who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, he said: I prayed with Abu Hurairah, and when he said the greatest, he remained silent for a while, then said: {Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds}"
"2861","(2861) Abu Al-Ahwas Salam bin Sulaym narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, on the authority of his father, he said: The Prophet said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: If one of you lies down and wants to pray, like the one at the back of a saddle, let him pray, and do not care. Who passed after that? (Abu Dawud 6851, Ibn Majah 940)"
"2862","(2862) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Hamid ibn Hilal, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said : The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When one of you stands up to pray, he will cover it if it is on his hands, such as The end of the journey.\n(Abu Dawud 702, Ahmad 1600, Ibn Khuzaymah 806)"
"2863","(2863) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to concentrate the battle on the day of Eid and pray for it. (Bukhari 973. Muslim 246)"
"2864","(2864) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Aoun ibn Abi Juhaif, on the authority of his father; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed to a goat, or one of her likenesses, and the road was behind her. (Bukhari 4991 Abu Dawud 688)"
"2865","(2865) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail ibn Umayyah, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: The war was only carried out. With the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to pray for her."
"2866","(2866) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, who said: I saw Omar focus A goat, then he prayed to it, while the goat passed between his hands."
"2867","(2867) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Abi Malik, on the authority of Abu Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abu Huraira, he said: He covers the person praying in his prayer like the back of a saddlebag with a whip wrapped around it."
"2868","(2868) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Muhallab ibn Abi Safariya, on the authority of a man from The Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If it is between you and those who pass by In your hands is like the back of a saddlebag, it will cover you."
"2869","(2869) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Abi Malik, on the authority of Abu Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to have war focused on him during the Eid, so he would lead her in prayer."
"2870","(2870) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: I saw Anas bin A landlord in the Sacred Mosque had set up a stick on which he prayed."
"2871","(2871) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: Al-Rabi’ ibn Khuthaym, when the heat was severe, would thrust his spear into the He went home, then prayed to him."
"2872","(2872) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Shuaib bin Al-Habhab, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, who said: The praying person covers what is behind the letter Knowledge"
"2873","(2873) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ma’dan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: If you pray in a space of the ground, so throw down your whip until you reach it."
"2874","(2874) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Thabit bin Qais Al-Ghaffari, Abu Al-Ghusn, who said: I saw Nafi’ bin Jubayr praying. To the whip when travelling, and to the stick."
"2875","(2875) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of cold, on the authority of alcohol; He said: A man covers himself during his prayer as if he were at the end of a saddle."
"2876","(2876) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Salam, on the authority of Al-Hasan and his followers, who said: She covers him like the end of a saddle when he is in front of the one praying."
"2877","(2877) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The river will cover you."
"2878","(2878) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to prefer it when they prayed in a space. To have in their hands what will cover them."
"2879","(2879) Zaid bin Hubab narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik bin Al-Rabi’ bin Sabra bin Ma’bad Al-Janni informed us, saying: My father told me, on the authority of his father, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Let one of you cover himself in your prayer, even if Peacefully\n(Ahmad 3/404, Ibn Khuzaymah 810)"
"2880","(2880) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Abi Ubaid, on the authority of Salamah, he said: I saw him setting stones In the wilderness, so if he wanted to pray, he prayed there."
"2881","(2881) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Saleh, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Ezza, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; He used to throw his whip, then pray to her."
"2882","(2882) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Al-Fadl and I came. On a donkey, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was leading the people in prayer, so we passed by some line, then we disembarked and left it to graze, and we did not Tell us something. (Muslim 362, Abu Dawud 715)"
"2883","(2883) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He prayed. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in a space with nothing between his hands."
"2884","(2884) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I asked Ata’ about a man who prays in space but does not have his hands on it. Something? He said: There is no harm in it."
"2885","(2885) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I saw Ibn Mughaffal praying while he was in the midst of the tribe. gap"
"2886","(2886) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Bakr, who said: I saw Al-Qasim and Salem praying while traveling. The desert beyond its cover."
"2887","(2887) Abdullah bin Idris, on the authority of Hisham, who said: My father used to pray without covering himself."
"2888","(2888) Sharik told us, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I saw Abu Ja’far and Amir praying across the street."
"2889","(2889) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mahdi bin Maimun, who said: I saw Al-Hasan praying in the cemetery, etc. cover"
"2890","(2890) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, who said: I saw Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah praying in a mosque in Minna. And the people were praying before him, then a young man from his family came and sat before him."
"2891","(2891) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, on the authority of Sahl bin Abi Hatham, may God be pleased with him, said: When one of you prays to a veil, let him close to it, and Satan will not interrupt his prayer."
"2892","(2892) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Sa’id. Al-Khudri, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: When one of you prays, let him pray to a cover and a city. And he does not let anyone pass between him or her. If someone passes by, let him fight him, for he is Satan.\n(Abu Dawud 698 and Ibn Hibban 2375)"
"2893","(2893) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, He said: Do not pray when there is a gap between you and the qiblah. Go forward to the qiblah, or cover yourself with a sarong."
"2894","(2894) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Umayyah, on the authority of Muslim ibn Abi Maryam, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: When he prays One of you should reach a curtain, and stay close to it, so that Satan does not pass in front of him."
"2895","(2895) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: When Ibn Umar did not find a way to One of the pillars of the mosque. He said to me: Let me have your back."
"2896","(2896) Mu`tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Salam, on the authority of his followers, who said: A man covers another man if he is sitting and praying."
"2897","(2897) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The man covers the person praying during prayer, and Ibn Sirin: The praying man should not cover himself."
"2898","(2898) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’; Ibn Umar used to have a man sit, and he would pray behind him while people passed in front of that man."
"2899","(2899) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mas’ar narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, he said: I asked Ibrahim, what is the sleeper’s cover? He said: No, I said: So the one sitting? He said: Yes."
"2900","(2900) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Abu Al-Waddak, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Nothing can interrupt the prayer, and repel it as much as you can, for he is Satan. (Abu Dawud 719. Daraqutni 368)"
"2901","2901) Abdi and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ali and Uthman. They said: It is not cut off. Prayer is one thing, and turn away from it as much as you can."
"2902","(2902) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem; It was said to Ibn Omar: Abdullah bin Ayash bin Abi Rabi’ah said: The donkey and the dog interrupt the prayer, so he said: No. Something interrupts a Muslim’s prayer."
"2903","(2903) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He said: Nothing interrupts the prayer, so defend yourselves."
"2904","(2904) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I have come and the credit is upon me. A donkey while the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was leading the people in prayer, according to his knowledge, so we passed by some of the row, and we disembarked and left it to graze. Tell us something."
"2905","(2905) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, who said: I asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab? He said: Nothing interrupts the prayer except a juvenile."
"2906","(2906) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan, on the authority of Ka’b bin Abdullah, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: No. Nothing interrupts the prayer, so avoid it as much as you can."
"2907","(2907) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Khathama, he said: I heard him speaking on the authority of lions, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Nothing interrupts the prayer except a black dog."
"2908","(2908) Abdou bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: He used to say: Nothing interrupts the prayer. Except disbelief."
"2909","(2909) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: Nothing interrupts the prayer, God is nearer to everything. Something"
"2910","(2910) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray during the night, and I was in the distance between him and the tribe, as an objection. The funeral (Muslim 2671, Ibn Majah 956)"
"2911","(2911) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Isolate your prayers as much as you can. The most fearful thing is the dog kennel."
"2912","(2912) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Nothing interrupts the prayer, but turn away from it what You were able"
"2913","(2913) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Hamid Ibn Hilal, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dhar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If there is not between his hands like the last part of the saddle, then it is He interrupted his prayer: a woman, a donkey, and a black dog. He said: I said: O Abu Dharr, what is the matter with the black dog compared to the dog? Red than yellow dog? He said: O nephew, I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, just as you asked me, and he said: The black dog is a devil."
"2914","(2914) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: A black, brown dog is a devil. And he interrupts the prayer."
"2915","(2915) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Muadh; Like him"
"2916","(2916) Abu Dawud and Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, who said: I heard Anas say: The prayer is interrupted by a woman, a donkey and a dog."
"2917","(2917) Abu Dawud and Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ziyad bin Fayyad, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas; Like him"
"2918","(2918) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of alcohol, who said: A woman, a donkey, and a dog interrupt a man’s prayer."
"2919","(2919) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Salam, on the authority of his leaders, who said: Ibn Abbas said: The black dog interrupts the prayer. And the menstruating woman. (Nasa’i 827)"
"2920","(2920) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Salam, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The prayer is interrupted by a dog and a woman. And the donkey."
"2921","(2921) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: A dog interrupts prayer. And the woman, and the pig, and the donkey, and the Jew, and the Christian, and the Magi. (Abu Dawud 704)"
"2922","(2922) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’a, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: A dog interrupts prayer. It was said to him: So the woman? He said: No, they are your brothers, your sisters and your mothers."
"2923","(2923) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Bakr; Ibn Umar repeated a rak’ah from a puppy that passed between his hands during prayer."
"2924","(2924) Shababi told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, who said: I heard Ata’ say: No one interrupts the prayer except a black dog. And the menstruating woman."
"2925","(2925) Muhammad bin Fudayl, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, he said: He was the son of Masoud: If someone passes by him while he is praying, he adheres to him until he returns him, and he says: He will interrupt half of his prayer. The passage of the esophagus between his hands."
"2926","(2926) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar and Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: If he passed between Your hand, do not return it."
"2927","(2927) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salim Abi al-Nadr, on the authority of Busr ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Abdullah Abi Hell, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If one of you knew what he had in the aisle between his brother’s hands And he prays. Meaning: from sin, to stop for forty. (Bukhari 510, Abu Dawud 701)"
"2928","(2928) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, who said: I heard Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman Omar bin Abdul Aziz worked, and a man passed by him while he was praying, and he pulled him to the point that he almost tore through his clothes. When he left, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: If the person passing through the hands of the praying person knew, he would like to His thigh is broken, and it does not pass through his hands."
"2929","(2929) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Khams, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraida, who said: My father saw people passing by, some of them passing by. between each other's hands during prayer, and he said: You will see these children, when they come to their senses, saying: We found our fathers like that. They do it."
"2930","(2930) Abu Muawiyah told us, Asim told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri was standing and praying. Then Abd al-Rahman bin al-Harith bin Hisham came and passed by him, so he pushed him away, but he refused to leave, so Abu pushed him away. Saeed put him down, and it was said to him: Are you doing this to Abd al-Rahman? He said: By God, if I refused but to take him by his hair, I would take it."
"2931","(2931) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If someone comes, he will pass between... Let him fight him, for he is nothing but a devil."
"2932","(2932) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: Abdullah said: Whoever is able If one of you does not pass between his hands while he is praying, let him do so, for what passes between the hands of the praying person is shorter than the one who passes. Aliyah"
"2933","(2933) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: I said to Saeed bin Jubayr: Should I let someone pass in front of me? He said: No, I said: If I refuse, he said: So what are you doing? I said: I have heard that Ibn Omar did not let anyone pass through him. He said: If you go, you will do the same as Ibn Omar. Your nose"
"2934","(2934) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying, and a young kid wanted to pass through the hands of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and proceeded forward until the kid appeared. (Abu Dawud 7091. Ahmad 1/291)"
"2935","(2935) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qais, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Umm Salama, she said: It was The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying, so he passed by Abdullah, or Omar bin Abi Salamah, and said: By his hand. So he returned, and Zainab, the son of Umm Salama, passed by, and he said: With such and such in his hand, so she left, and when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed He greeted him and said: They are most likely. (Ahmad 6/294)"
"2936","(2936) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar Sulayman bin Hayyan told us, on the authority of Sulayman Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: He took the initiative The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told him or her to pass through his hands. (Tabarani 4965)"
"2937","(2937) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Abd al-Aziz al-Tanukhi narrated to us, on the authority of a servant of Yazid bin Nimran, on the authority of Yazid bin Nimran said: I saw a man crippled, and he said: I passed in front of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while I was riding a donkey. While he was praying, he said: Oh God, cut off his tracks, so I did not walk on them. (Abu Dawud 7061. Ahmad 4/377)"
"2938","(2938) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, who said: It passed between the hands of Ibn Umar while he was in Prayer, so he rose from his seat, then pushed into my chest."
"2939","(2939) Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Huraim told us, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Bura, he said: I have never seen anyone more severe. He must pass between his hands a prayer from Ibrahim al-Nakhi and Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad."
"2940","(2940) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wa’il ibn Hajar; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat, so he bent the left one and placed the right one, meaning in prayer."
"2941","(2941) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hussein Al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Badil, on the authority of Abu Al-Jawzai, on the authority of Aisha, She said: Whenever the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrated and raised his head, he would not prostrate until he was completely seated, and he was He spreads his left leg, and sets up his right leg."
"2942","(2942) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Zubayr ibn Adiyy, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was When the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, sits during prayer, he spreads his left leg until the backs of his feet turn black. (Abu Dawud 45. Abdul Razzaq 3037)"
"2943","(2943) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt, who said: The Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He spreads the left foot, and sets up the right."
"2944","(2944) Ibn Fudail and Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah On the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: It is part of the Sunnah of prayer to spread the left side flat, and to place the right side straight. (Bukhari 827. Abu Dawud 45)"
"2945","(2945) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadhra, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: When you sit, spread your feet. The left one, for it is more worthy of your prayer and of your crucifixion."
"2946","(2946) Waki’ and Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali; He used to set up the right side and spread out the left side."
"2947","(2947) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He might have laid down all of his feet, Perhaps he made the right person lie down and put the left one in the position. Whenever Muhammad sat, the right-hand man would lie down and the left-hand man would lie down."
"2948","(2948) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhall, on the authority of Ibrahim; Like the saying of Muhammad."
"2949","(2949) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Khalil prohibited me from My chin is like the chin of a monkey. (Bukhari 1981, Muslim 85)"
"2950","(2950) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali; He disliked slowing down in prayer, and said: It is the obstacle of Satan."
"2951","(2951) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali; He disliked standing still in prayer."
"2952","(2952) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari, who said: I prayed next to my father. So I stood up on the tops of my feet, and he pulled me until I felt comfortable."
"2953","(2953) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated oppression and turmoil."
"2954","(2954) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad; He hated to pause in prayer."
"2955","(2955) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; He disliked standing between the two prostrations."
"2956","(2956) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hussein Al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Badil, on the authority of Abu Al-Jawzai, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to forbid the punishment of Satan."
"2957","(2957) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: It is Sunnah to place your buttocks on Your heels in prayer. (Tirmidhi 283. Abu Dawud 841)"
"2958","(2958) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, and Abu Sa’id; They were standing between the two prostrations."
"2959","(2959) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: He used to kneel between the two prostrations."
"2960","(2960) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Atiyya, who said: I saw the servants standing in prayer between The two prostrations, meaning Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, Ibn Omar, and Ibn Abbas."
"2961","(2961) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: I saw Atiyya standing between the two prostrations, so I said to him, and he said: I saw Ibn Umar, Ibn Abbas, and Ibn al-Zubayr falling between the two prostrations."
"2962","(2962) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Saqif bin Bishr Al-Ijli, who said: I saw a peacock sitting between four Rak’ahs when he sits."
"2963","(2963) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Musa al-Tahan, who said: I saw a mujahid standing between the two prostrations."
"2964","(2964) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far; He used to sit on his heels between the two prostrations."
"2965","(2965) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; When he sat, he would bend his feet."
"2966","(2966) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri; He was praying while the mirror was passing by him, right and left, so he saw no harm in that. He said: And Ibn Sirin was She got up in her shoes, he swam in them."
"2967","(2967) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mughirah narrated to us, on the authority of Abraham; He saw no harm in a woman passing by, to the right of the man and to his left, while he was praying."
"2968","(2968) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I asked Ata’ about him? He did not see any harm in it. He said: Someone who asked Abraham and he disapproved of him told me."
"2969","(2969) Abbad bin Al-Awwam narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, he said: Maymunah narrated to me, she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was praying while I was wearing his shoes, so his garment might have touched me when he prostrated, and he was He prays over the veil."
"2970","(2970) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: Musab bin Saad narrated to me, he said: It was The shoe before Saad was a coffin, and the servant used to come and take what she needed from his right, and from his left she would not be cut off. His prayers"
"2971","(2971) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Ghayath, who said: I asked Al-Hasan about a woman passing beside a man while he is praying? He said: There is no problem unless you help him."
"2972","(2972) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: It was disliked for a woman to pray. In a man’s shoes when he is praying."
"2973","(2973) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abu Masoud, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: A prayer in which a man does not straighten his crucifixion, bowing and prostrating, is not sufficient. \n(Abu Dawud 581, Ahmad 4/122)"
"2974","(2974) Mulazim bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Badr, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Ali bin Shayban narrated to me, on the authority of His father, Ali bin Shayban, who was part of the delegation, said: We went out until we came to the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So we pledged allegiance to him and prayed with him, but he noticed with the back of his eye a man who did not straighten his spine when bowing or prostrating, so when he had finished The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O community of Muslims, there is no prayer for one who does not straighten his spine when bowing and prostrating.\n(Ahmad 4/23. Ibn Hibban 2202)"
"2975","(2975) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Ali bin Yahya bin Khallad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His uncle, who was Badri, said: We were sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a man entered and prayed a light prayer, not He performed bowing or prostration, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at him while we were not aware. He said: So he prayed, then he came and gave the salutation. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, responded to him and said: Repeat, for you have not prayed. He said: So he did that, three times, all of that. He said to him: Repeat, for you have not prayed. When it was the fourth hour, he said: O Messenger of God, teach me, for by God I have tried hard. He said: When you stand up to pray, face the qiblah, then say “Allahu Akbar”, then recite, then bow, until you are at ease while bowing, then Raise until you are at ease standing, then prostrate until you are at ease prostrating, then sit until you are at ease sitting, then stand. If you do that Your prayer has been completed, and whatever you lack from that, you diminish your prayer.\n(Abu Dawud 856. Ahmad 4/340)"
"2976","(2976) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ubaid Allah bin Omar told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; That a man entered the mosque and prayed, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in the direction of the mosque, so he came and greeted him, and said: To him: And upon you, go back and pray, for you have not yet prayed. So he came back and greeted him, and said: Go back, for you have not prayed yet. So he said to him: The man in the third: Teach me, O Messenger of God. He said: When you stand up for prayer, perform ablution thoroughly, then face the Qiblah. So say “Allahu Akbar”, then recite whatever is easy for you from the Qur’an, then bow until you are confident in your bowing, then rise until you are standing upright, then Prostrate until you are secure in your prostration, then rise until you are standing upright, or he said: sitting, then do that in all of your prayers. (Bukhari 6667 and Muslim 298)"
"2977","(2977) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ali bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abi Saeed Al-Khudri; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The worst of people is the one who steals your prayer. They said: O Messenger of God, How can he steal it? He said: Neither bowing nor prostration is complete. (Ahmad 3/56, Abu Ali 1306)"
"2978","(2978) Shababah bin Siwar narrated to us, saying: Sulaiman bin Al-Mughirah narrated to us, saying: Thabit narrated to us, on the authority of Anas, he said: He described We have a memory of the Prophet’s prayer, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he stood up to pray, bowed, raised his head from bowing, and remained standing. Until some of us thought that he had forgotten. He said: Then he prostrated and sat straight until some of us thought that he had forgotten.\n(Bukhari 821, Muslim 195)"
"2979","(2979) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Salem Al-Barrad, who said: We came to Abu Masoud Al-Ansari about home, so we said to him: Tell us about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so he stood up to pray in front of us, so when He knelt down and placed his palms on his knees, and placed his fingers below that, and brought his elbows together until all of them were level. Some of it, then he raised his head, then said: God hears whoever praises Him, so he stood up until all of it was leveled, then he prostrated and did so. For example, he prayed two rak'ahs, and when he completed them, he said: This is how we saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying."
"2980","(2980) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The man He will pray for sixty years, and no prayer will be accepted for him. He may complete the bowing, but not complete the prostration, and he may complete the prostration, and not complete the prostration. Kneeling"
"2981","(2981) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja`far al-Ansari, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, who said: I saw Abu Hamid Al-Saadi with ten of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So he said to them: Shall I not speak to you? On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? They said: Come, he said: I saw him when he raised his head from bowing, he remained standing until every bone fell into place, then he lowered himself. prostrating and saying “Allahu Akbar”"
"2982","(2982) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, and Yazid bin Harun, on the authority of Hussein Al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Badil, on the authority of Abu Al-Jawza’i, on the authority of Aisha, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, bowed, he did not bow his head, nor did he He straightens it, but it is between that. If he raises his head from bowing, he does not prostrate until he is completely standing, and if he prostrates, he raises He did not prostrate his head until he was completely sitting, and he would say the greeting between every two rak'ahs."
"2983","(2983) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd bin Wahhab, on the authority of Hudhayfah; He entered the mosque and saw a man praying near him from the gates of Canada. He did not complete the bowing and prostration, so when he left, Hudhayfy said to him: How long has this been your prayer? He said: Forty years ago, and Hudhayfy said: You have not prayed for forty years, and if you had died with this prayer, you would have died in a different manner. The nature that was created upon Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then he went to him and taught him, and said: The man is to lighten his sins. The prayer is performed by bowing and prostrating. (Bukhari 891. Ahmad 5/384)"
"2984","(2984) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, the worst People stole the one who stole his prayers. They said: O Messenger of God, how could he steal your prayers? He said: Neither bowing nor prostration is complete."
"2985","(2985) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu An-Nadr Muslim, who said: I heard Hamla bin Abdul Rahman, he said: He saw His servants saw a man who could not fully bow or prostrate, so he took him by the hand, and the man was frightened, and his servants said: Do not resemble this man, and do not With examples like him, no prayer is sufficient except according to the Mother of the Book."
"2986","(2986) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Al-Qasim ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Ja’far; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw a man bowing his head while prostrating, and he said: If this and that died His prayers, he died in a religion other than that. (Bukhari 2690, Ibn Khuzaymah 665)"
"2987","(2987) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Yahya, on the authority of his father; That Abu Hurairah saw a woman praying while she was beating, so he said: You lied."
"2988","(2988) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Qur’a, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Sa’eed bin Al-Musayyab saw a man praying but not completing it. His bowing, nor his prostration, so he counted it and said: Your prayer has ended."
"2989","(2989) Waki’ told us, he said: I heard Al-A’mash saying: I saw Anas bin Malik in Mecca standing and praying at the Kaaba. So when I showed him, he said: He was standing and praying straight in his prayer, so when he raised his head, he would stand up until it was straight. The furrows of his stomach"
"2990","(2990) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abi Farwa, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, he said: He entered the mosque A man prayed a prayer that did not complete the bowing or prostration. He said: I mentioned that to Abdullah bin Zayd, and he said: Because it is better than abandoning it."
"2991","(2991) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Al-Miswar bin Makhramah; He saw a man who could not complete his bowing or prostration, so he said to him: Repeat, but he refused, so he did not leave him until he repeated it."
"2992","(2992) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Musa bin Muslim, who said: A man came to pray while a peacock was sitting, but he did not perform the bowing. Nor prostration. Some of the people said: What is the point of this prayer? Tawus said: No, and part of it will be recorded for him according to what he performed."
"2993","(2993) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Yahya bin Ubaid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid; He was asked about a man who neither bowed nor prostrated completely? He said: It is better than nothing."
"2994","(2994) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Amr Al-Mala’i, on the authority of Abu Qais, on the authority of Masruq; He saw a man praying, and he saw him raising his feet while he was prostrating, and he said: This man’s prayer was not complete."
"2995","(2995) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Majliz; He saw a prostrating man who had raised one of his legs, and said: God made them six, and you made them five."
"2996","(2996) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Salman Al-Farisi, He said: Prayer is a measure, so whoever fulfills it, Allah will fulfill it for him, and you know what God said regarding the measure: {Woe to those who give up}."
"2997","(2997) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Farafasa, on the authority of the one who mentioned him, on the authority of Abu Alderaa; He passed by a man who did not complete the bowing or prostration, and he was told, and Abu Darda’ said: Something is better than nothing."
"2998","(2998) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Mufaddal bin Mihalil, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Qays; Bilal saw a man who did not complete the bowing or prostration, so he said: If this man died, he would die following a religion other than Jesus, son of Maryam."
"2999","(2999) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Al-Hurr, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Mukhaymara, he said: He took my hand, He said: Abdullah took him by the hand, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took him by the hand and taught me the tash-hud: Greetings to God. And the prayers and good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God’s mercy and blessings be upon him. Peace be upon us and the servants of God. The righteous, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.\n(Ahmad 1/450. Ibn Hibban 1963)"
"3000","(3000) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: We used to pray behind the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, so we say: Peace be upon God before His servants, peace be upon Gabriel, peace be upon Michael, peace be upon so-and-so and so-and-so. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made the decision, he said: Indeed, God is peace, so when one of you sits in prayer, let him say: Greetings to God and prayers and good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God’s mercy and blessings be upon you. Peace be upon us and the servants of God is the righteous, I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, then choose. (Bukhari 6230 and Muslim 302)"
"3001","(3001) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayed, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah; Such as the hadith of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, regarding the tash-hud. (Ahmad 1/413, Tabarani 9931)"
"3002","(3002) Hushaym told us, saying: Husayn bin Abdul Rahman, Mughirah, and Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: When we sat behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace during prayer, we would say: Peace be upon God, peace be upon Gabriel. Peace be upon Mikael, peace be upon so-and-so and so-and-so. He said: Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, turned to us and said: Indeed, God And it is peace, so say: Greetings are to God and prayers and good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God’s mercy and blessings be upon you. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. You are If you do that, then you have greeted every righteous servant in the heavens and the earth.\n(Bukhari 7381, Muslim 302)"
"3003","(3003) Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Saif bin Abi Sulaiman told us, he said: I heard Mujahid say: Abdullah told me. Ibn Sakhbara, he said: I heard Ibn Masoud say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught me the Tashahid. Enough is enough. It is sufficient, as the surahs from the Qur’an teach me: greetings are to God, prayers and good things, peace be upon you, O Prophet. May God’s mercy and blessings be upon him, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad His servant and Messenger, and he was among us. When he was arrested, we said: Peace be upon the Prophet. (Bukhari 6245. Muslim 59)"
"3004","(3004) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught me May God’s peace and blessings be upon you. The Tashahhud: greetings to God, prayers and good things. May the peace and blessings of God be upon you, O Prophet. And His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant. And His Messenger.\n(Ahmad 1/376)"
"3005","(3005) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed, he said: His leaders narrated to me, on the authority of Yunus bin Jubayr, on the authority of Hattan bin Abdullah On the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: If it is while sitting, let it be as one of you says: Good greetings and prayers to God, peace be upon you, O Prophet, and may God have mercy on him, peace be upon us and the righteous servants of God, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger."
"3006","(3006) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ayman, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He used to say: In the name of God, and by God, greetings are to God, and prayers are to God, peace be upon you, O Prophet, and his mercy. God and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant. And His Messenger, I ask God for Paradise, and I seek refuge in God from Hell. (Ahmad 5/363, Ibn Majah 902)"
